WEBVTT

1
00:01:20.422 --> 00:01:22.130
Stop the vehicle immediately.

2
00:01:22.922 --> 00:01:24.130
Stop it right there.

3
00:01:25.088 --> 00:01:26.297
I repeat, pull over.

4
00:01:29.505 --> 00:01:32.338
I am giving you a direction
to stop the vehicle.

5
00:01:32.505 --> 00:01:35.463
Failure to comply with my direction
is an offense.

6
00:01:35.797 --> 00:01:37.047
Stop the tractor.

7
00:01:37.838 --> 00:01:40.005
You are under arrest for trespass

8
00:01:40.088 --> 00:01:41.672
and theft of a conveyance.

9
00:01:42.297 --> 00:01:44.297
Stop being a dickhead and pull over.

10
00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.172
I can't, mate.
I'm trying to get to the airport.

11
00:01:59.088 --> 00:02:00.213
OK, OK.

12
00:02:05.672 --> 00:02:08.047
Ahh!

13
00:02:11.838 --> 00:02:12.838
Sorry.

14
00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.922
My dad has a saying.

15
00:02:24.047 --> 00:02:25.672
A lie begins in the soul

16
00:02:26.047 --> 00:02:27.672
and then travels the world.

17
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.255
There have been three lies
that have shaped my life.

18
00:02:35.338 --> 00:02:39.297
The first is the one that saved
my father's life before I was born.

19
00:02:41.255 --> 00:02:43.380
Mahdi! Baathists! Run!

20
00:02:43.672 --> 00:02:45.755
Mother, go!

21
00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.838
Mahdi, come with us.

22
00:02:47.922 --> 00:02:49.130
I can't leave my mother.

23
00:02:49.422 --> 00:02:50.713
Mother, you must go!

24
00:02:52.213 --> 00:02:53.338
No, take me!

25
00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:55.463
-He's a good boy.
-Mother, no!

26
00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.297
Leave her!

27
00:03:01.588 --> 00:03:05.463
He was arrested by Saddam Hussein's men
for opposing the dictator.

28
00:03:09.338 --> 00:03:10.880
He would have been killed,

29
00:03:12.005 --> 00:03:15.213
had it not been for his friends
posing as prison guards.

30
00:03:16.797 --> 00:03:17.630
Mahdi.

31
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.755
They escaped
by crossing the border to Iran.

32
00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.047
Surely, that was a good lie?

33
00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.380
I mean, without it,

34
00:03:39.463 --> 00:03:41.297
I wouldn't even be here today.

35
00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:45.463
The second lie was us believing

36
00:03:45.547 --> 00:03:47.880
we could have a life as Iraqis in Iran.

37
00:03:47.963 --> 00:03:49.130
Whoa, Ali, look.

38
00:03:49.505 --> 00:03:50.838
Persian girls are hot.

39
00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.172
Move over. My turn.

40
00:03:55.547 --> 00:03:56.588
Did you see that?

41
00:03:56.755 --> 00:03:58.213
She just flashed me.

42
00:03:58.297 --> 00:04:00.380
You godless Arab donkey!

43
00:04:00.588 --> 00:04:02.755
She fell into my eye, I promise!

44
00:04:04.838 --> 00:04:06.172
Ali, look over there.

45
00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:07.797
Where? I can't see anything.

46
00:04:07.922 --> 00:04:09.172
Behind the door.

47
00:04:12.172 --> 00:04:14.338
God! She has red hair!

48
00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:19.005
You lying Arab donkey. Again?
I should send you back to Saddam!

49
00:04:19.088 --> 00:04:22.172
I wasn't looking! I swear on the Prophet!

50
00:04:22.255 --> 00:04:25.547
Eventually, we realized
we were never going to make it in Iran.

51
00:04:27.088 --> 00:04:29.630
We have just flown out of Iranian airspace

52
00:04:29.713 --> 00:04:32.047
and can now serve alcohol in all cabins.

53
00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.963
So please, sit back and enjoy
our in-flight service to Melbourne.

54
00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.380
So it begins.

55
00:04:43.588 --> 00:04:45.005
Swap.

56
00:04:46.088 --> 00:04:48.880
This leads to my third lie,
my biggest lie.

57
00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:52.505
Do I look like someone who eats bacon?

58
00:04:52.588 --> 00:04:54.630
And as you and God are my witnesses...

59
00:04:54.713 --> 00:04:56.630
Come Judgment Day, you answer.

60
00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:58.880
Today, this lie must end.

61
00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:01.880
Today, I will tell you the whole truth.

62
00:05:19.755 --> 00:05:21.005
Prayer has started.

63
00:05:21.088 --> 00:05:23.088
Kill them, Bombers! Kill them!

64
00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:26.922
God be with you, Watson. Run!

65
00:05:27.422 --> 00:05:29.922
-Goal!
-Yes, come on Bombers.

66
00:05:30.005 --> 00:05:31.588
Ali, study.

67
00:05:33.213 --> 00:05:36.380
-Mineralocorticoids...
-God is with us!

68
00:05:36.797 --> 00:05:37.630
Om Hassan.

69
00:05:38.588 --> 00:05:39.755
Remember Yaqoub,

70
00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:40.797
from my village?

71
00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.922
Mustafa found him here,
in the detention center.

72
00:05:44.213 --> 00:05:45.713
Yaqoub knows the guy

73
00:05:45.797 --> 00:05:48.672
who supplies my cousin Jaasem’s shop
in Basra.

74
00:05:48.755 --> 00:05:50.547
Beep beep. Mafia coming through.

75
00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.088
-Om Hassan.
-Wait, Mohammed.

76
00:05:53.172 --> 00:05:56.088
-Mum, don't worry.
-What are you doing?

77
00:05:56.172 --> 00:05:58.672
The supplier told Yaqoub he...

78
00:05:59.672 --> 00:06:00.588
Om Hassan.

79
00:06:01.005 --> 00:06:01.838
Please listen.

80
00:06:02.422 --> 00:06:04.463
The supplier told Yaqoub,

81
00:06:04.922 --> 00:06:06.088
he saw my mother.

82
00:06:08.755 --> 00:06:10.255
My mother. Alive.

83
00:06:11.463 --> 00:06:13.047
-Still alive?
-In Basra.

84
00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.463
-Grandmother is alive?
-Ali, study.

85
00:06:16.297 --> 00:06:17.338
Thank God.

86
00:06:17.505 --> 00:06:19.838
I may finally have a mother-in-law.

87
00:06:19.922 --> 00:06:20.755
God willing.

88
00:06:22.297 --> 00:06:23.547
One week to go, son.

89
00:06:24.963 --> 00:06:26.630
Keep doing what you're doing.

90
00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.547
You will reap rewards.

91
00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:29.963
Come on, Bombers.

92
00:06:30.047 --> 00:06:31.172
Top student.

93
00:06:31.255 --> 00:06:33.672
-Prayer has started.
-This is the last quarter.

94
00:06:33.755 --> 00:06:36.588
-What's this?
-Adult science. You wouldn't know it.

95
00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.213
What is it?

96
00:06:38.463 --> 00:06:40.672
If you must know, it's the pancreas.

97
00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.213
-Om Hassan.
-Lucky guess.

98
00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.547
Go away, Ramona.

99
00:06:44.838 --> 00:06:46.588
♪ Tick tock, tick tock♪

100
00:06:46.797 --> 00:06:47.922
♪ Will you pass?♪

101
00:06:48.588 --> 00:06:49.505
♪ Will you not?♪

102
00:06:49.588 --> 00:06:51.047
Tackle.

103
00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:51.963
Baba.

104
00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.297
Bring your mother
and your costume for the play.

105
00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.922
Why did we choose the Bombers?
All they do is tear my heart apart.

106
00:06:59.463 --> 00:07:00.297
Like you.

107
00:07:14.005 --> 00:07:17.047
In the time of the Bani Umayyah empire,

108
00:07:17.463 --> 00:07:20.797
the prince and his treasurer
were walking along,

109
00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:23.797
when they came across an old man,

110
00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.380
planting a date seed.

111
00:07:25.463 --> 00:07:30.922
This date seed will only bear fruit
after your death.

112
00:07:32.213 --> 00:07:33.588
What will you gain?

113
00:07:34.963 --> 00:07:37.297
Old men have planted before me

114
00:07:37.922 --> 00:07:40.297
and I have eaten their fruit.

115
00:07:40.588 --> 00:07:42.922
The prince was very moved by this.

116
00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.130
He turned to his treasurer and said...

117
00:07:45.213 --> 00:07:48.088
Wow, old man, you are so--

118
00:07:48.172 --> 00:07:50.422
Ali, son. No improvising, please.

119
00:07:50.505 --> 00:07:51.338
Sorry.

120
00:07:53.088 --> 00:07:54.130
Sister, please.

121
00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.963
-And replied:
-Exalted one. You suggest...

122
00:07:59.047 --> 00:08:02.088
Jamal's parents came last week
to ask for her hand,

123
00:08:02.797 --> 00:08:04.922
and they did not get to drink the tea.

124
00:08:05.005 --> 00:08:06.422
-Mum.
-What?

125
00:08:06.505 --> 00:08:07.588
Thank you, Yomna.

126
00:08:07.672 --> 00:08:10.838
The prince turned to his treasurer

127
00:08:10.922 --> 00:08:13.255
signaling for another purse.

128
00:08:13.338 --> 00:08:15.088
I'm signaling for another purse.

129
00:08:15.172 --> 00:08:17.963
But this time his treasurer
put up his hand and said:

130
00:08:18.047 --> 00:08:19.963
Enough wisdom.

131
00:08:20.172 --> 00:08:23.380
This damn date seed
will bankrupt our kingdom.

132
00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:32.422
He thinks this place
is a theater for making jokes,

133
00:08:33.422 --> 00:08:36.713
and they pay him,
and I'm the one driving a taxi.

134
00:08:36.797 --> 00:08:37.880
Brothers and sisters.

135
00:08:40.005 --> 00:08:42.838
We do not know what fruit
our seeds will bear.

136
00:08:44.422 --> 00:08:45.880
But if our hearts

137
00:08:45.963 --> 00:08:48.422
and intentions are pure,

138
00:08:49.797 --> 00:08:53.547
the rewards can be
a thousand times what we expect.

139
00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:06.505
Auditions for this year's musical

140
00:09:06.588 --> 00:09:08.922
will be held after Friday prayer.

141
00:09:10.797 --> 00:09:14.088
Will we encore our hit show,
The Prophet's Last Battle?

142
00:09:14.172 --> 00:09:15.297
I still know my lines.

143
00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.463
Hajjina, we have been singing
about the Prophet's battle

144
00:09:18.547 --> 00:09:20.005
for three years now.

145
00:09:21.047 --> 00:09:24.047
This year, inshallah,
I will write a more...

146
00:09:24.672 --> 00:09:25.922
contemporary musical.

147
00:09:26.005 --> 00:09:28.005
I'm tingling with anticipation.

148
00:09:28.088 --> 00:09:30.297
The Trial of Saddam Hussein.

149
00:09:33.213 --> 00:09:34.422
It will be comedy.

150
00:09:34.922 --> 00:09:37.380
The man caused us so much pain.

151
00:09:38.088 --> 00:09:40.338
Believe me, now he will make us laugh.

152
00:09:43.088 --> 00:09:44.172
What brilliance.

153
00:09:44.255 --> 00:09:45.380
Sheikhna!

154
00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:48.130
You follow in the steps of a great man.

155
00:09:48.713 --> 00:09:51.630
May you draw upon his wisdom
for your exam.

156
00:09:58.588 --> 00:09:59.630
-Ayoob.
-Yeah.

157
00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:00.755
That's her.

158
00:10:01.047 --> 00:10:01.880
Who?

159
00:10:03.255 --> 00:10:04.755
I'm going to talk to her.

160
00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:05.963
Not here.

161
00:10:07.297 --> 00:10:08.130
Ali, no.

162
00:10:14.713 --> 00:10:17.422
I'll get the jumper leads from my car.
I'll help you.

163
00:10:17.505 --> 00:10:19.255
Yes, please. Jumper leads.

164
00:10:19.338 --> 00:10:20.797
OK. Thank you very much.

165
00:10:20.922 --> 00:10:21.755
Thank you.

166
00:10:24.047 --> 00:10:25.713
Will you be wanting milk tonight?

167
00:10:27.713 --> 00:10:29.547
Ali, my boy,

168
00:10:30.422 --> 00:10:32.547
I missed your father's wisdom?

169
00:10:32.922 --> 00:10:33.963
Just by an hour.

170
00:10:35.547 --> 00:10:38.463
It's not my fault. I blame my wives.

171
00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.380
Especially that one.

172
00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:42.588
The tall one.

173
00:10:43.088 --> 00:10:46.880
She has to stop for Nando's,

174
00:10:47.463 --> 00:10:51.005
and she left the damn headlights on.

175
00:10:52.463 --> 00:10:53.505
What are you doing?

176
00:10:54.588 --> 00:10:55.422
Ali.

177
00:10:57.963 --> 00:10:59.297
Eyes here.

178
00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.005
Jumper leads!

179
00:11:06.547 --> 00:11:09.838
I hope you're ready for the big exam,
son of the cleric.

180
00:11:11.005 --> 00:11:13.380
Jumper leads!

181
00:11:13.797 --> 00:11:16.380
-Man, you won't get into medicine.
-Yes, I will.

182
00:11:16.463 --> 00:11:18.963
-I got a degree in science, didn't I?
-Just.

183
00:11:19.047 --> 00:11:21.213
They gave him a science degree too.

184
00:11:22.297 --> 00:11:25.797
Yeah, but he hasn't spent the last year
studying for the entrance exam.

185
00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:26.713
Have you?

186
00:11:26.797 --> 00:11:29.922
Look man, I'm physically, emotionally
and spiritually ready

187
00:11:30.005 --> 00:11:31.713
to sit this goddamn exam.

188
00:11:31.797 --> 00:11:33.422
Do you even want to do medicine?

189
00:11:33.505 --> 00:11:34.963
He has to sit the exam.

190
00:11:35.047 --> 00:11:37.672
I'm a forklift driver.
My father makes me sit the exam.

191
00:11:37.755 --> 00:11:39.880
Except I'm smart enough
to know I'm stupid.

192
00:11:39.963 --> 00:11:41.463
-Put it back.
-Twinnies.

193
00:11:41.922 --> 00:11:44.088
I don't want to know. Reseal it.

194
00:11:44.172 --> 00:11:45.338
Hey, is that the one?

195
00:11:47.297 --> 00:11:48.130
Oh yeah.

196
00:11:48.755 --> 00:11:51.088
Tonight's the night.
I'm going to talk to her.

197
00:11:51.172 --> 00:11:53.922
-You already did.
-Yeah, we had a great conversation.

198
00:11:54.005 --> 00:11:55.797
-But this is the next level.
-Ali.

199
00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.297
Don't do the stupid voice. No one gets it.

200
00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:21.130
Good evening.

201
00:12:22.672 --> 00:12:24.338
I see you came for the milk.

202
00:12:25.338 --> 00:12:27.630
And I've got something special
to show you.

203
00:12:27.963 --> 00:12:29.588
Or a special that we have.

204
00:12:30.005 --> 00:12:32.172
The Chupa Chups. They're on special.

205
00:12:33.213 --> 00:12:35.380
Not a special. Ten for five dollars.

206
00:12:36.088 --> 00:12:38.547
So if I spend $50,
you'd give me 100?

207
00:12:39.797 --> 00:12:41.588
We don't have that many in stock.

208
00:12:41.755 --> 00:12:43.422
It's a pity. That's all I wanted.

209
00:12:44.672 --> 00:12:47.422
Do you need a hand carrying these
to your father's shop?

210
00:12:49.463 --> 00:12:51.255
-It's two bottles.
-So you're OK?

211
00:12:51.338 --> 00:12:52.172
Yeah, I'm OK.

212
00:12:54.797 --> 00:12:59.547
Are you sure
you don't want the president of Iraq

213
00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.880
to help you carry the milk bottles?

214
00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:08.922
Dictator.

215
00:13:12.172 --> 00:13:14.088
That was Saddam Hussein's voice.

216
00:13:14.922 --> 00:13:17.422
-You can Google it.
-I don't think I will be.

217
00:13:18.297 --> 00:13:21.963
-You sitting the medical entrance exam?
-Yeah. I'm going to be a doctor.

218
00:13:23.588 --> 00:13:24.422
Charlie.

219
00:13:24.505 --> 00:13:27.713
My name's Ali, but this is
the Aussie version, so it's Charlie.

220
00:13:27.797 --> 00:13:30.005
Yeah, I know who you are,
son of the cleric.

221
00:13:30.088 --> 00:13:31.713
And I know who you are, Dianne.

222
00:13:31.797 --> 00:13:33.922
You're the daughter
of the fish and chip man.

223
00:13:34.005 --> 00:13:37.047
Thanks. It's how I like to be remembered.

224
00:13:37.922 --> 00:13:39.797
Just put it on the account, will you?

225
00:13:43.047 --> 00:13:44.088
-Hooroo!
-Sayonara!

226
00:13:44.172 --> 00:13:45.088
Salaam alaikum!

227
00:13:45.297 --> 00:13:48.380
You idiots. You just ruined it for me.

228
00:13:48.463 --> 00:13:49.713
Yeah, I ruined it for you.

229
00:13:49.797 --> 00:13:51.713
It wasn't the Saddam voice
that killed it.

230
00:13:51.797 --> 00:13:54.963
-You need to get married, like me.
-You got married by mistake.

231
00:13:55.047 --> 00:13:57.338
-Did you knock her up?
-It's a damn tea ceremony.

232
00:13:57.422 --> 00:13:58.255
It's a minefield.

233
00:13:58.338 --> 00:14:01.380
Turks do it different to Persians.
They do it different to us.

234
00:14:01.463 --> 00:14:05.005
-How do you guys do it?
-It doesn't matter. The sex is the same.

235
00:14:05.088 --> 00:14:06.547
Unbelievable, man.

236
00:14:06.963 --> 00:14:09.755
And my wife reckons
I'm starting to get the hang of it.

237
00:14:09.963 --> 00:14:11.213
You animal.

238
00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.130
Retroperitoneal...

239
00:14:24.005 --> 00:14:25.380
Baba?

240
00:14:26.005 --> 00:14:28.130
-Thinking about your big exam?
-Of course.

241
00:14:30.213 --> 00:14:31.047
I found this.

242
00:14:32.172 --> 00:14:33.255
Hassan's initials.

243
00:14:34.547 --> 00:14:37.463
I put it on when
he won the math prize in Abadan.

244
00:14:38.547 --> 00:14:39.588
I remember that.

245
00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.130
He would have made a great doctor.

246
00:14:45.047 --> 00:14:48.963
It may not bring you luck,
but it might bring you comfort.

247
00:14:53.047 --> 00:14:54.297
Come. Breakfast.

248
00:15:12.213 --> 00:15:13.755
Cinema? Are you crazy?

249
00:15:14.713 --> 00:15:15.755
It's genius!

250
00:15:17.672 --> 00:15:20.547
We join a random family
and sit next to their daughters.

251
00:15:21.088 --> 00:15:22.588
What if the film is no good?

252
00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:27.922
Who cares about the film? Girls!

253
00:15:28.505 --> 00:15:30.338
Ali, look at what I found!

254
00:15:43.213 --> 00:15:44.047
[land mine clicks[

255
00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:54.713
Ali!

256
00:16:30.255 --> 00:16:31.088
Charlie.

257
00:16:32.297 --> 00:16:33.130
Hey.

258
00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.297
You never told me you were doing medicine.

259
00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.297
Didn't know I needed your permission.

260
00:16:38.838 --> 00:16:41.338
No, I mean we could have studied together.

261
00:16:44.505 --> 00:16:45.338
Pst.

262
00:16:46.797 --> 00:16:48.130
I got your Chupa Chups in.

263
00:16:48.713 --> 00:16:50.713
I'm about to do a seven-hour exam.

264
00:16:50.963 --> 00:16:51.880
Stop talking.

265
00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:56.463
Ali.

266
00:16:57.922 --> 00:16:58.797
Hey, Luay.

267
00:16:59.922 --> 00:17:00.755
Good luck.

268
00:17:01.838 --> 00:17:03.172
Yeah, you too.

269
00:17:33.797 --> 00:17:35.838
Baba habib.

270
00:17:42.963 --> 00:17:46.005
My leader,
you are gracious to spare this time.

271
00:17:47.047 --> 00:17:49.547
-For such a foolish man.
-Please, Hajjina.

272
00:17:49.963 --> 00:17:51.588
Ali will serve as witness.

273
00:17:52.838 --> 00:17:55.588
What are you doing?
That's my racket, you idiot.

274
00:17:55.838 --> 00:18:00.088
We must all take a leaf
out of this family's book.

275
00:18:00.172 --> 00:18:03.172
Your children have self-respect.

276
00:18:03.255 --> 00:18:06.838
This house is exactly
as we have come to know of the Prophet.

277
00:18:06.922 --> 00:18:09.755
We are all beneath God's wide...

278
00:18:10.463 --> 00:18:12.255
generous shadow, but...

279
00:18:13.338 --> 00:18:14.172
Please.

280
00:18:15.005 --> 00:18:16.338
-To your issue.
-Sheikhna.

281
00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:19.797
The last day of Ramadan,

282
00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:22.797
I coached soccer all day.

283
00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:25.505
No water, no food. 100 degrees.

284
00:18:25.588 --> 00:18:27.880
And I come home
and she has burnt the lamb.

285
00:18:29.713 --> 00:18:31.880
The baklava is like concrete.

286
00:18:34.088 --> 00:18:35.797
Tea, Haj?

287
00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.880
Even within this house
there is the occasional angry word.

288
00:18:41.172 --> 00:18:42.172
No, my leader.

289
00:18:43.005 --> 00:18:46.005
In my anger, I divorced her three times.

290
00:18:46.338 --> 00:18:48.213
-You said the words three times?
-More.

291
00:18:48.422 --> 00:18:49.255
It was more.

292
00:18:50.922 --> 00:18:53.505
Unfortunately,
you are from the Hanafi faith

293
00:18:53.588 --> 00:18:54.880
and once you say to God,

294
00:18:54.963 --> 00:18:57.255
"I divorce my wife," three times...

295
00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.755
there is no going back.

296
00:18:59.838 --> 00:19:02.797
I lost the most beautiful woman
in the world

297
00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.880
over a piece of baklava.

298
00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.380
To be clear.

299
00:19:18.338 --> 00:19:20.922
When you uttered the words,
"I divorce you,"

300
00:19:21.005 --> 00:19:23.963
did you say, "I divorce you,"
and then have a shower?

301
00:19:24.672 --> 00:19:27.838
And then come out and say it again?

302
00:19:28.047 --> 00:19:31.297
And take a walk,
and say it again for a third time?

303
00:19:31.422 --> 00:19:35.255
I said it all in one terrible moment,

304
00:19:35.338 --> 00:19:37.005
that will haunt me for eternity.

305
00:19:38.005 --> 00:19:40.588
So, it was one thought.

306
00:19:41.755 --> 00:19:42.672
A continuum.

307
00:19:43.588 --> 00:19:44.505
A singularity.

308
00:19:44.755 --> 00:19:46.422
What do you mean, my leader?

309
00:19:46.672 --> 00:19:49.130
In soccer, when Ali kicks a goal,

310
00:19:49.755 --> 00:19:52.172
the crowd cry, "Goal, goal, goal!"

311
00:19:52.255 --> 00:19:54.713
But how many goals has Ali kicked?

312
00:19:55.588 --> 00:19:57.088
-One.
-One thought.

313
00:19:58.463 --> 00:19:59.963
One divorce.

314
00:20:05.505 --> 00:20:09.463
Go to your wife
and commit to her with all your heart.

315
00:20:09.838 --> 00:20:11.047
Even to the baklava.

316
00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.713
You have saved my family.

317
00:20:19.005 --> 00:20:21.880
May you grow in his shadow

318
00:20:21.963 --> 00:20:23.463
and guide us all,

319
00:20:23.547 --> 00:20:25.547
and with a good wife by your side.

320
00:20:27.005 --> 00:20:28.338
See you at rehearsals, Ali.

321
00:20:29.505 --> 00:20:32.213
♪ Sheikh has once again saved my life♪

322
00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:34.922
♪ Now I get to go back to my wife♪

323
00:20:35.005 --> 00:20:36.713
Can you make your own laws, Dad?

324
00:20:37.422 --> 00:20:38.255
Believe me.

325
00:20:38.338 --> 00:20:41.088
Even the Prophet
would not have wanted a divorce.

326
00:20:41.588 --> 00:20:43.755
No man is complete without marriage.

327
00:20:45.213 --> 00:20:46.047
But tell me.

328
00:20:46.755 --> 00:20:47.922
How was your exam?

329
00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:49.713
Good.

330
00:20:49.838 --> 00:20:51.880
-You got a top mark?
-Guaranteed.

331
00:20:56.547 --> 00:20:58.213
Have you told Dad you're fucked?

332
00:20:58.297 --> 00:20:59.963
You won't even get 80, man.

333
00:21:00.047 --> 00:21:03.088
You don't know that for sure.
I answered all the questions.

334
00:21:03.505 --> 00:21:04.838
You know I love you, bro?

335
00:21:04.922 --> 00:21:07.005
Stop pretending
you're like the old man.

336
00:21:07.588 --> 00:21:09.797
You and I both know
we'll never be as good as him.

337
00:21:10.922 --> 00:21:14.088
Johnno, you fucking dickhead.
You're cleaning that, asshole.

338
00:21:14.172 --> 00:21:15.005
Mohammed.

339
00:21:15.463 --> 00:21:18.297
This is my job, Dad.
I have to speak Australian.

340
00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:21.630
Get me the fucking keys
to the car you were meant to put there.

341
00:21:22.255 --> 00:21:23.088
Please.

342
00:21:31.172 --> 00:21:32.005
Dad.

343
00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:34.963
We're meant to believe in miracles?
They do happen?

344
00:21:36.047 --> 00:21:36.963
There is a riddle.

345
00:21:37.047 --> 00:21:38.922
A bridge is about to collapse.

346
00:21:39.297 --> 00:21:41.088
Any weight, it would crumble...

347
00:21:43.338 --> 00:21:44.463
What is this?

348
00:21:46.797 --> 00:21:48.172
Your temporary transport.

349
00:21:57.422 --> 00:21:59.005
Hey, mate. Don't put it in.

350
00:22:06.963 --> 00:22:08.672
Please God, prove your existence.

351
00:22:33.172 --> 00:22:34.005
Hey, Ali.

352
00:22:34.297 --> 00:22:35.838
Ali, hurry.

353
00:22:36.547 --> 00:22:40.838
Seyyed Ghaffar has thrown a barbecue party
for his son.

354
00:22:41.672 --> 00:22:44.047
Young Luay got 96 for his exam!

355
00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:47.172
96,2. But what is a number?

356
00:22:47.505 --> 00:22:50.255
I'm sure your family will throw
an even bigger celebration.

357
00:22:51.547 --> 00:22:53.963
I have to speak to my father.
Is he inside?

358
00:22:54.297 --> 00:22:56.797
Our leader is giving brother Qais comfort.

359
00:22:56.880 --> 00:22:58.963
Marital problems.

360
00:22:59.047 --> 00:23:01.380
-Finally, someone who's not a taxi driver.
-Please.

361
00:23:01.463 --> 00:23:04.463
My son and I are merely slaves of God.

362
00:23:04.755 --> 00:23:06.588
If my son becomes a doctor,

363
00:23:07.505 --> 00:23:09.047
and serves this community,

364
00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:13.547
it is not because of my genes
or my endless hours of schooling.

365
00:23:14.297 --> 00:23:15.130
It is...

366
00:23:16.213 --> 00:23:17.047
Him.

367
00:23:22.463 --> 00:23:24.380
Ali. My good friend.

368
00:23:25.797 --> 00:23:28.172
University of Melbourne,
here we come.

369
00:23:28.505 --> 00:23:30.130
96,2, huh?

370
00:23:30.463 --> 00:23:33.672
Maybe we should not be so vocal
in our celebration.

371
00:23:34.755 --> 00:23:38.672
We must remember,
not all can bask under God's glory

372
00:23:39.713 --> 00:23:43.005
I bet you Ali did extremely well.

373
00:23:44.047 --> 00:23:46.797
-I bet the same.
-If the Prophet hadn't banned gambling...

374
00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:48.672
I would bet my entire house

375
00:23:48.755 --> 00:23:51.005
that Ali would have a higher score
than Luay.

376
00:23:57.713 --> 00:23:58.547
So...

377
00:23:59.505 --> 00:24:01.588
-Enlighten us, Ali.
-Come on, Ali. Tell us.

378
00:24:01.672 --> 00:24:03.922
-The suspense is tingling me.
-Let's hear it.

379
00:24:04.005 --> 00:24:06.588
There is no man alive
smarter than his father.

380
00:24:06.672 --> 00:24:07.630
Maybe only his son.

381
00:24:11.047 --> 00:24:12.338
I got 96 also.

382
00:24:15.297 --> 00:24:16.213
Point 4.

383
00:24:16.922 --> 00:24:18.255
I would have won a house.

384
00:24:40.630 --> 00:24:41.463
Baba.

385
00:24:41.922 --> 00:24:43.130
What is this I hear?

386
00:24:44.755 --> 00:24:47.297
What is this they are saying
at the mosque?

387
00:24:49.630 --> 00:24:51.547
Ninety-six point four.

388
00:24:54.255 --> 00:24:56.088
Praise be to God.

389
00:24:56.172 --> 00:24:58.130
Ninety-six point four!

390
00:24:58.547 --> 00:25:01.297
I was worried you'd struggle to get 90.

391
00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:03.505
All the years fighting in the war,

392
00:25:03.588 --> 00:25:06.505
dragging my family
from one hell to another...

393
00:25:06.588 --> 00:25:09.213
My dumb brother is a genius.

394
00:25:09.713 --> 00:25:12.755
My brother's a genius. A genius.

395
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:14.838
My dumb brother's a genius.

396
00:25:14.922 --> 00:25:16.713
Handsome son.

397
00:25:16.797 --> 00:25:20.922
- You are too gorgeous to be a doctor.
- Yes? I'm with him now.

398
00:25:21.005 --> 00:25:22.630
Here's to rid the evil eye.

399
00:25:23.797 --> 00:25:24.630
Mum.

400
00:25:25.172 --> 00:25:29.172
We have also ordered a dozen sheep
from the abattoir, as an offering.

401
00:25:29.255 --> 00:25:30.672
Oh, no.

402
00:25:30.755 --> 00:25:32.963
I don't want the sheep to die
for no reason.

403
00:25:33.047 --> 00:25:34.797
-No reason?
-Free them instead.

404
00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:36.880
Wait until everyone hears back home.

405
00:25:36.963 --> 00:25:40.047
Hears that my son is finally a doctor.

406
00:25:40.130 --> 00:25:42.630
♪ Where's my brother, Ali?
You'll find him in the library♪

407
00:25:42.713 --> 00:25:45.213
- ♪ You'll find him in the library♪
- Guys, just one second.

408
00:25:45.297 --> 00:25:46.338
Please, be quiet.

409
00:25:46.422 --> 00:25:47.755
Be quiet!

410
00:25:49.338 --> 00:25:51.547
I don't want to make a big deal
out of this.

411
00:25:52.297 --> 00:25:54.547
You, no fuss. No fuss.

412
00:25:56.213 --> 00:25:59.672
The next student is Jamal Hilfi.

413
00:25:59.755 --> 00:26:00.963
Unbelievable, man.

414
00:26:01.047 --> 00:26:03.297
I thought you were as dumb as me.
I got 68,9.

415
00:26:03.588 --> 00:26:05.297
Your father must be over the moon.

416
00:26:05.380 --> 00:26:07.797
...accepted into the paramedic course.

417
00:26:12.338 --> 00:26:17.505
Paramedic may sound like a fancy name
for nurses driving vans,

418
00:26:18.047 --> 00:26:23.255
but more important
is that we serve the Almighty Creator.

419
00:26:23.713 --> 00:26:26.088
Next to sit the entrance exam,

420
00:26:26.463 --> 00:26:30.005
this humble slave's very own son, Luay.

421
00:26:30.505 --> 00:26:32.838
A score of 96,2.

422
00:26:39.463 --> 00:26:43.672
And easily accepted into medicine
at Melbourne University.

423
00:26:48.338 --> 00:26:50.588
Luay, you are his holy seed.

424
00:26:50.672 --> 00:26:52.672
Next on the list is Ayoob Maithan.

425
00:26:53.505 --> 00:26:54.338
Oh dear.

426
00:26:55.922 --> 00:26:59.963
Ayoob... with a score of 68,9.

427
00:27:05.713 --> 00:27:07.088
No gift for you, Ayoob.

428
00:27:09.005 --> 00:27:11.797
Some of our sisters are on the list too,

429
00:27:11.880 --> 00:27:14.880
and one of them has achieved a...

430
00:27:15.047 --> 00:27:16.047
reasonable score.

431
00:27:16.130 --> 00:27:18.463
Indeed. 99,1.

432
00:27:18.880 --> 00:27:21.172
Wow. Mashallah. Praise be to God.

433
00:27:21.255 --> 00:27:25.130
She's also been accepted into medicine
at Melbourne University,

434
00:27:25.213 --> 00:27:28.380
and if her father is willing
to turn his back

435
00:27:28.463 --> 00:27:30.297
from the way of the Prophet

436
00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:33.963
and let her go to the university
and mix with Westerners...

437
00:27:35.130 --> 00:27:37.130
I hear she wears ripped jeans.

438
00:27:37.213 --> 00:27:40.005
-And our revered cleric's son...
-My son is next. Get ready.

439
00:27:40.088 --> 00:27:42.422
...got a score of 96,4.

440
00:27:42.963 --> 00:27:45.797
Good on you, Ali,
and to everyone who succeeded.

441
00:27:48.463 --> 00:27:52.047
Congratulations to our sisters
on their scores.

442
00:27:52.130 --> 00:27:53.630
Notably, our top student.

443
00:27:53.713 --> 00:27:56.713
And if you were my daughter,
I would be very proud.

444
00:28:06.172 --> 00:28:07.505
Ali! Number one!

445
00:28:07.922 --> 00:28:09.380
He's a tiger!

446
00:28:09.547 --> 00:28:11.047
He's a wolf!

447
00:28:11.213 --> 00:28:12.255
He's a lion!

448
00:28:12.338 --> 00:28:13.380
A speech!

449
00:28:13.797 --> 00:28:15.130
Top student!

450
00:28:15.755 --> 00:28:18.213
Looking at your face is worship.

451
00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:22.005
The greatest son of the greatest cleric!

452
00:28:23.547 --> 00:28:26.005
Brothers and sisters...
Don't use the echo.

453
00:28:29.547 --> 00:28:30.880
Brothers and sisters.

454
00:28:31.547 --> 00:28:32.797
First of all,

455
00:28:33.463 --> 00:28:36.088
I must congratulate our sister,

456
00:28:36.297 --> 00:28:37.838
the true top student.

457
00:28:37.922 --> 00:28:40.047
-But you!
-You're a genius, bro.

458
00:28:40.422 --> 00:28:41.672
Brothers and sisters.

459
00:28:42.213 --> 00:28:44.880
Surely, we are all equal.

460
00:28:46.547 --> 00:28:49.213
There's a funny thing
that the English say.

461
00:28:49.297 --> 00:28:50.630
"You say potato,

462
00:28:50.713 --> 00:28:52.005
I say pot-ah-to."

463
00:28:52.213 --> 00:28:55.213
Let's say, for example, I got 96,4...

464
00:28:55.630 --> 00:28:58.172
or 68,5.

465
00:28:58.713 --> 00:28:59.838
That could never happen!

466
00:28:59.922 --> 00:29:01.505
I would have won a house!

467
00:29:05.755 --> 00:29:07.338
Brothers, what I mean is,

468
00:29:07.422 --> 00:29:09.797
I'd be the same person
standing before you today.

469
00:29:09.880 --> 00:29:10.797
Flesh and blood.

470
00:29:11.297 --> 00:29:13.338
My heart would still pump blood--

471
00:29:13.422 --> 00:29:16.713
Already he enlightens us
with medical terminology.

472
00:29:26.838 --> 00:29:27.838
Thank you.

473
00:29:29.380 --> 00:29:32.880
♪ Ali, you are the son of the cleric♪

474
00:29:33.338 --> 00:29:35.880
♪ And through your father's noble blood♪

475
00:29:36.213 --> 00:29:39.380
♪ You will do medicine♪

476
00:29:39.755 --> 00:29:43.922
♪ And fill us out free prescriptions♪

477
00:29:45.922 --> 00:29:46.880
Tell me,

478
00:29:46.963 --> 00:29:49.297
if you had a patient who was a Jew...

479
00:29:49.380 --> 00:29:51.130
-Would you treat him?
-Of course.

480
00:29:51.213 --> 00:29:52.838
Good. Good boy!

481
00:29:53.838 --> 00:29:55.630
What is most important to you?

482
00:29:55.713 --> 00:29:58.088
Intelligence, appearance,
or cleaning skill?

483
00:29:58.172 --> 00:29:59.463
-What?
-Apart from wealth.

484
00:29:59.547 --> 00:30:01.380
As a doctor, you will make great money.

485
00:30:01.463 --> 00:30:03.755
Forget it, I will sort it out.
Cleaning, I think.

486
00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:04.838
Ask him, father.

487
00:30:05.838 --> 00:30:06.672
Ali baba.

488
00:30:08.713 --> 00:30:10.630
We need a copy of your results.

489
00:30:10.713 --> 00:30:12.588
Not because we doubt you,

490
00:30:12.672 --> 00:30:16.463
but we want to frame it
and decorate the mosque with your glory.

491
00:30:29.130 --> 00:30:30.255
You failed, didn't you?

492
00:30:34.505 --> 00:30:36.088
I got 68,5.

493
00:30:41.755 --> 00:30:43.880
-You have to tell Dad.
-Are you crazy?

494
00:30:44.505 --> 00:30:46.005
It'll destroy the family.

495
00:30:46.088 --> 00:30:48.088
-Dad's reputation.
-Am I crazy?

496
00:30:48.172 --> 00:30:50.463
You just told
the biggest lie in the world.

497
00:30:50.547 --> 00:30:51.922
What were you thinking?

498
00:30:54.880 --> 00:30:56.380
I'm the smart one, like Dad.

499
00:30:56.463 --> 00:30:57.963
I'm going to be the doctor.

500
00:30:58.047 --> 00:31:00.130
You're the idiot
who has to sort this out.

501
00:31:13.047 --> 00:31:13.880
What was that?

502
00:31:14.338 --> 00:31:15.172
What?

503
00:31:25.463 --> 00:31:26.922
Come on. That all you've got?

504
00:31:40.838 --> 00:31:42.463
Hey. The queen.

505
00:31:43.505 --> 00:31:44.838
99,1, huh?

506
00:31:44.922 --> 00:31:46.797
Potato, pot-ah-to. What's in a score?

507
00:31:46.963 --> 00:31:47.797
Well done.

508
00:31:48.088 --> 00:31:50.047
See, I knew you were brilliant.

509
00:31:50.922 --> 00:31:52.338
You're our top student.

510
00:31:52.422 --> 00:31:53.922
-Really? You think that?
-Yeah.

511
00:31:54.005 --> 00:31:55.755
Well done and a million well dones.

512
00:31:55.838 --> 00:31:58.255
Hey, we're going to do medicine together.

513
00:31:58.463 --> 00:31:59.755
I won't be doing it.

514
00:32:00.213 --> 00:32:01.047
Why not?

515
00:32:03.213 --> 00:32:04.088
Your dad, right?

516
00:32:04.172 --> 00:32:07.713
I told him our community needed
a Muslim to look after our women, but...

517
00:32:07.797 --> 00:32:08.630
he won't move.

518
00:32:09.047 --> 00:32:10.047
Di, we've got to go.

519
00:32:10.130 --> 00:32:13.672
Look, he'd have a heart attack
if he found out I played basketball.

520
00:32:22.880 --> 00:32:23.922
You know, Charlie?

521
00:32:24.005 --> 00:32:28.047
You and your dad were the only ones
that congratulated me on my score.

522
00:32:28.755 --> 00:32:29.672
Come on, D.

523
00:32:36.463 --> 00:32:37.297
Dianne.

524
00:32:38.880 --> 00:32:39.713
Yeah?

525
00:32:41.172 --> 00:32:42.672
Yeah, I did that already.

526
00:32:47.088 --> 00:32:48.672
-How are you? Good?
-All right.

527
00:32:48.755 --> 00:32:50.213
Five potato cakes, thanks.

528
00:32:52.172 --> 00:32:53.672
How is our beloved cleric?

529
00:32:54.297 --> 00:32:55.880
He's starting to get the aches,

530
00:32:55.963 --> 00:32:58.088
but as soon as I'm a doctor, I'll fix him.

531
00:32:58.172 --> 00:32:59.963
Perhaps you will fix me too?

532
00:33:00.047 --> 00:33:02.422
My shoulder, my knee...
You don't want to know.

533
00:33:02.505 --> 00:33:05.255
Yeah, and Western doctors
don't understand the Arab body.

534
00:33:05.338 --> 00:33:06.255
They know nothing.

535
00:33:07.505 --> 00:33:09.047
Stop bowling wides.

536
00:33:10.213 --> 00:33:11.547
How many runs are we chasing?

537
00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:17.047
Do you have a doctor in the family?

538
00:33:20.588 --> 00:33:22.463
Only my wife's family in Mesr.

539
00:33:23.338 --> 00:33:24.297
In Egypt.

540
00:33:26.005 --> 00:33:27.505
Rest her soul.

541
00:33:28.338 --> 00:33:29.172
And here...

542
00:33:29.672 --> 00:33:30.880
I only have my daughter.

543
00:33:31.255 --> 00:33:33.380
Then you need to find someone.

544
00:33:33.463 --> 00:33:34.297
Urgent.

545
00:33:34.380 --> 00:33:35.255
My Uncle Adnan...

546
00:33:35.338 --> 00:33:38.172
He was written off
by every Western doctor in the country,

547
00:33:38.255 --> 00:33:40.213
but praise be to God,

548
00:33:40.297 --> 00:33:42.130
his niece devoted her life to him.

549
00:33:42.213 --> 00:33:43.672
She studied medicine...

550
00:33:44.463 --> 00:33:45.755
Now, you should see him.

551
00:33:46.130 --> 00:33:48.630
He's a tennis coach, fit like a bull.

552
00:33:49.172 --> 00:33:53.422
LBW. Useless.
Bloody bludger and useless.

553
00:33:53.505 --> 00:33:54.338
Ali.

554
00:33:58.880 --> 00:34:00.713
You know the universities here.

555
00:34:02.130 --> 00:34:03.505
How do they say...

556
00:34:05.005 --> 00:34:06.047
Horny boys.

557
00:34:09.255 --> 00:34:10.297
You understand?

558
00:34:11.713 --> 00:34:13.005
I'll be going to the same uni.

559
00:34:13.713 --> 00:34:16.963
I could watch out for her.
Tell you if I see anything.

560
00:34:27.213 --> 00:34:28.047
Ali.

561
00:34:30.005 --> 00:34:31.088
Your potato cakes.

562
00:34:32.963 --> 00:34:34.463
Do you want chicken salt?

563
00:34:38.755 --> 00:34:39.588
So...

564
00:34:39.963 --> 00:34:42.922
My mother relocated
from Basra to Najaf?

565
00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:44.213
To Najaf?

566
00:34:45.505 --> 00:34:46.338
No?

567
00:34:48.880 --> 00:34:50.505
-To Baghdad.
-To Baghdad.

568
00:34:51.713 --> 00:34:53.172
-What's he saying?
-That's why.

569
00:34:53.255 --> 00:34:55.713
Is Faiq going to see her,
or is he sending someone?

570
00:34:55.797 --> 00:34:57.380
My mother is in Baghdad, where?

571
00:34:57.463 --> 00:34:58.922
Get him to hire a car and drive.

572
00:34:59.005 --> 00:35:00.380
-Say again.
-It's only 500.

573
00:35:00.463 --> 00:35:02.588
I can hardly hear you.
Please, say it again.

574
00:35:02.672 --> 00:35:05.172
Ali, cut the noise.
Your father can't hear anything.

575
00:35:05.255 --> 00:35:06.797
Om Hassan, I can't hear anything

576
00:35:06.880 --> 00:35:09.255
because I have a mad woman
standing next to me.

577
00:35:09.338 --> 00:35:10.463
-Talk.
-Faiq?

578
00:35:11.713 --> 00:35:12.547
Hello?

579
00:35:13.630 --> 00:35:14.463
Hello?

580
00:35:15.255 --> 00:35:16.213
Hello?

581
00:35:16.297 --> 00:35:17.255
I lost the line.

582
00:35:21.672 --> 00:35:22.505
Try again.

583
00:35:23.713 --> 00:35:25.047
Dad, maybe I should drive.

584
00:35:25.380 --> 00:35:27.797
It has a sport gearbox
and an unusual clutch.

585
00:35:28.297 --> 00:35:29.255
Turn right here.

586
00:35:29.713 --> 00:35:31.130
Dad, I have to tell you.

587
00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:32.463
I'm not as...

588
00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:36.005
-I'm not as clever as everybody thinks.
-I apologize!

589
00:35:36.755 --> 00:35:38.838
I didn't know you owned the road.

590
00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:41.922
This has been the week from God.

591
00:35:42.588 --> 00:35:45.297
My mother is alive,
the play will begin soon,

592
00:35:45.380 --> 00:35:47.588
and you are to be a doctor.

593
00:35:47.672 --> 00:35:49.547
No, Dad. What I meant...

594
00:35:49.630 --> 00:35:51.422
Dad, can you get out of first?

595
00:35:51.755 --> 00:35:53.713
No, we are here.

596
00:35:55.588 --> 00:35:57.797
Give Barbie back her car, you wanker.

597
00:35:57.880 --> 00:35:59.338
Good on you, mate.

598
00:35:59.463 --> 00:36:01.922
If only God would let me
raise it back at you.

599
00:36:02.297 --> 00:36:05.172
Dad, the mechanic's back that way.
What are we doing here?

600
00:36:05.255 --> 00:36:07.422
There are many paths in life, Ali.

601
00:36:07.588 --> 00:36:08.672
Sheikhna.

602
00:36:09.505 --> 00:36:11.380
-Hajjina.
-Wow.

603
00:36:16.255 --> 00:36:18.713
-What a surprise.
-A surprise indeed.

604
00:36:18.797 --> 00:36:20.630
You know our daughter, Yomna.

605
00:36:21.463 --> 00:36:23.463
She is, as you describe her...

606
00:36:23.547 --> 00:36:25.338
The pride of your eye.

607
00:36:26.005 --> 00:36:27.755
This is the doctor in the flesh.

608
00:36:28.338 --> 00:36:29.172
Say hello.

609
00:36:31.005 --> 00:36:31.838
Hello.

610
00:36:33.172 --> 00:36:34.005
G'day.

611
00:36:35.255 --> 00:36:37.380
Dad, you're in a "No Standing" zone.

612
00:36:37.588 --> 00:36:38.422
We are sitting.

613
00:36:38.963 --> 00:36:40.588
-Sheikhna.
-Hajjina.

614
00:36:42.630 --> 00:36:44.422
I'll see you at training, Ali.

615
00:36:46.005 --> 00:36:46.838
Wow.

616
00:36:48.505 --> 00:36:50.422
She's nice, don't you think?

617
00:36:51.422 --> 00:36:53.088
I don't know, Dad. Probably.

618
00:36:53.880 --> 00:36:54.713
Yeah.

619
00:36:57.422 --> 00:36:58.755
What did I press here?

620
00:37:25.880 --> 00:37:26.713
Where's Dad?

621
00:37:27.463 --> 00:37:28.880
-I have to speak to him.
-No.

622
00:37:29.005 --> 00:37:31.130
-I have to tell him the truth.
-Ali, no.

623
00:37:31.213 --> 00:37:32.088
Hey, Dad.

624
00:37:33.963 --> 00:37:36.213
He's just learned his mother has died.

625
00:37:40.588 --> 00:37:41.422
Oh, Dad.

626
00:37:42.880 --> 00:37:44.255
She had a heart attack.

627
00:37:45.963 --> 00:37:48.672
It would have been nice
if she knew I was still alive.

628
00:37:48.755 --> 00:37:50.880
She knew. I'm sure she knew.

629
00:37:52.172 --> 00:37:54.172
Come, let's give your father some space.

630
00:37:56.713 --> 00:37:58.088
That really sucks, Dad.

631
00:38:05.422 --> 00:38:08.505
To God we belong and to Him we return.

632
00:38:19.547 --> 00:38:22.297
She would have been so proud of you, son.

633
00:38:49.380 --> 00:38:52.213
-You're seriously doing this?
-I can make this work.

634
00:38:52.922 --> 00:38:55.297
I'll sit in all the lectures,
study for a year,

635
00:38:55.380 --> 00:38:57.338
resit the exam fully prepared.

636
00:38:58.380 --> 00:38:59.380
You're an idiot.

637
00:39:05.422 --> 00:39:06.255
Baba Ali.

638
00:39:09.672 --> 00:39:11.005
Let the journey begin.

639
00:39:12.463 --> 00:39:14.505
Go and return with health my son.

640
00:39:18.338 --> 00:39:20.047
Yeah, lots of healthy shit, bro.

641
00:39:21.172 --> 00:39:22.005
Good luck.

642
00:39:24.172 --> 00:39:25.005
Thanks, guys.

643
00:39:59.922 --> 00:40:00.838
Hello, Charlie.

644
00:40:02.922 --> 00:40:03.755
The queen.

645
00:40:04.672 --> 00:40:06.213
All hail. You made it.

646
00:40:06.838 --> 00:40:08.172
I wanted to thank you.

647
00:40:10.047 --> 00:40:11.505
It's because of you I'm here.

648
00:40:11.588 --> 00:40:14.838
Every Arab man has a medical condition
he wants looked into.

649
00:40:14.922 --> 00:40:17.880
Mind you, I have to find a cure
for arthritis by the end of the year.

650
00:40:17.963 --> 00:40:18.797
No pressure.

651
00:40:20.755 --> 00:40:22.505
I should go in.

652
00:40:24.547 --> 00:40:25.380
Ali.

653
00:40:28.713 --> 00:40:29.547
Luay.

654
00:40:30.713 --> 00:40:31.547
Shall we?

655
00:40:33.255 --> 00:40:34.088
We shall.

656
00:40:35.630 --> 00:40:38.672
The plasmalemma,
otherwise termed the cell membrane,

657
00:40:38.755 --> 00:40:42.005
is composed of phospholipids, proteins,

658
00:40:42.088 --> 00:40:44.338
glycolipids, and cholesterol.

659
00:40:44.797 --> 00:40:48.338
The plasmalemma
is called the phospholipid bilayer

660
00:40:48.880 --> 00:40:51.547
because its phospholipids
have two distinct layers,

661
00:40:52.672 --> 00:40:56.297
and the molecules lie
so that the heads are at the surface

662
00:40:56.380 --> 00:40:58.297
and the tails are on the inside.

663
00:41:00.505 --> 00:41:04.630
♪ I'm down in a hole
You ask me why? ♪

664
00:41:04.755 --> 00:41:08.588
♪ Smoking ganja and getting high♪

665
00:41:08.713 --> 00:41:11.588
♪ Getting high
Getting high♪

666
00:41:11.672 --> 00:41:14.422
♪ It all started with a lie♪

667
00:41:14.505 --> 00:41:17.922
♪ Go, America
F you, goodbye♪

668
00:41:18.005 --> 00:41:20.380
♪ Getting high
Getting high♪

669
00:41:20.463 --> 00:41:22.755
♪ Our president is getting high♪

670
00:41:22.838 --> 00:41:24.130
Stop there, please. Stop.

671
00:41:24.880 --> 00:41:25.713
Very good.

672
00:41:26.838 --> 00:41:29.547
I think we need to make
the dance less suggestive.

673
00:41:29.630 --> 00:41:31.630
Can I speak with the Baathists, please?

674
00:41:31.713 --> 00:41:34.130
Sheikhna, should I shave the beard?

675
00:41:35.547 --> 00:41:38.380
Allahu Akbar. I am Saddam...

676
00:41:38.713 --> 00:41:39.547
Ali.

677
00:41:41.713 --> 00:41:44.297
So what did you think of today's...

678
00:41:45.463 --> 00:41:48.047
immunoglobulin genetic diversity lecture?

679
00:41:48.463 --> 00:41:50.463
I found it...

680
00:41:52.047 --> 00:41:52.880
intense.

681
00:41:56.297 --> 00:41:58.172
You know, we might...

682
00:41:58.588 --> 00:42:00.547
travel to uni together sometimes?

683
00:42:00.630 --> 00:42:01.547
Swap notes?

684
00:42:02.838 --> 00:42:03.672
Great.

685
00:42:03.838 --> 00:42:04.755
Test each other.

686
00:42:06.713 --> 00:42:07.547
Great.

687
00:42:15.797 --> 00:42:16.630
Thank you.

688
00:42:30.630 --> 00:42:31.463
After you.

689
00:42:31.588 --> 00:42:33.213
No, after you.

690
00:42:33.297 --> 00:42:34.713
But, you're to my right.

691
00:42:36.213 --> 00:42:37.588
Now you're to my right.

692
00:42:37.672 --> 00:42:38.755
But, you...

693
00:42:40.130 --> 00:42:42.505
You two dancing, or are you in this tute?

694
00:42:43.463 --> 00:42:44.297
Yeah.

695
00:42:45.255 --> 00:42:47.297
No, they swapped me over into this so...

696
00:42:56.588 --> 00:42:59.505
I am looking for my son, the doctor.
Ali Albasri.

697
00:42:59.588 --> 00:43:00.422
Call him for me.

698
00:43:02.213 --> 00:43:05.463
You know how we've been talking,
student to student?

699
00:43:06.130 --> 00:43:10.297
I thought maybe we could talk
male to female, you know? Speak speak.

700
00:43:10.922 --> 00:43:13.255
I mean, not now, but when you're ready.

701
00:43:14.422 --> 00:43:16.463
How would you know when I'm ready?

702
00:43:17.963 --> 00:43:18.797
Morning all.

703
00:43:19.005 --> 00:43:19.963
Morning.

704
00:43:20.047 --> 00:43:20.880
Right, everyone.

705
00:43:21.380 --> 00:43:23.838
-Alicia, here, is Patient X.
-Hi.

706
00:43:23.922 --> 00:43:27.172
I need a volunteer
to take her case history.

707
00:43:27.797 --> 00:43:28.797
You. Briefcase.

708
00:43:30.047 --> 00:43:31.588
Your face is not familiar.

709
00:43:33.463 --> 00:43:35.172
Yeah, I was swapped over.

710
00:43:36.380 --> 00:43:37.213
Ali.

711
00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:40.088
OK, Ali. Come down.

712
00:43:44.630 --> 00:43:48.422
This is a 26-year-old female

713
00:43:48.505 --> 00:43:50.255
who comes into the GP Clinic.

714
00:43:51.380 --> 00:43:53.922
You're a second-year GP intern.

715
00:43:54.880 --> 00:43:55.963
Take her history.

716
00:43:56.047 --> 00:43:58.088
-So, I'm the doctor?
-You're the doctor.

717
00:44:00.880 --> 00:44:03.088
-Good afternoon, Alicia.
-Afternoon.

718
00:44:03.172 --> 00:44:05.005
Thanks for coming to my clinic.

719
00:44:06.297 --> 00:44:08.922
What seems to be the problem
this afternoon?

720
00:44:09.547 --> 00:44:11.505
I have a really weird discharge.

721
00:44:14.797 --> 00:44:15.630
Huh.

722
00:44:16.297 --> 00:44:17.422
That's no good.

723
00:44:19.797 --> 00:44:20.630
Not good.

724
00:44:21.713 --> 00:44:25.338
What do you mean, he's not on the list?
He was first at the mosque to get in.

725
00:44:25.422 --> 00:44:28.005
-I'll find him myself.
-Sorry, you can't go in there.

726
00:44:28.088 --> 00:44:30.047
So with the discharge,

727
00:44:30.130 --> 00:44:33.547
did you see it first,
smell it, or hear it?

728
00:44:34.588 --> 00:44:36.422
I saw it, and then I smelled it,

729
00:44:36.505 --> 00:44:37.838
but it didn't make a noise.

730
00:44:39.672 --> 00:44:41.005
Come.

731
00:44:41.505 --> 00:44:42.463
Oh, shit.

732
00:44:42.547 --> 00:44:46.380
No wonder we couldn't find him.
He is operating. See?

733
00:44:47.255 --> 00:44:49.047
These people say they don't know you.

734
00:44:49.255 --> 00:44:51.922
-Is this your teacher?
-Sorry. Family emergency.

735
00:44:52.005 --> 00:44:54.630
-Is he a good teacher?
-He's one of the greats, Mum.

736
00:44:54.755 --> 00:44:56.547
OK. Back up here.

737
00:44:56.755 --> 00:44:58.672
Our two families are having tea.

738
00:44:58.963 --> 00:45:00.255
You need to dress up.

739
00:45:05.130 --> 00:45:07.297
Hello, Ayoob? Hey, bro.

740
00:45:07.922 --> 00:45:11.088
With this tea ceremony,
what do I do not to get married?

741
00:45:11.172 --> 00:45:12.630
Spoon in? Spoon out?

742
00:45:12.713 --> 00:45:14.630
Do I drink the tea? Not drink the tea?

743
00:45:14.713 --> 00:45:16.713
Relax... but listen carefully.

744
00:45:16.797 --> 00:45:18.505
So, you grab the sugar.

745
00:45:19.047 --> 00:45:22.297
-I thought ours didn't have the sugar?
-No, it does. Oh, wait...

746
00:45:23.047 --> 00:45:24.963
Look, forget the sugar for the moment.

747
00:45:25.047 --> 00:45:28.213
The most important thing
is when you drink the tea...

748
00:45:28.297 --> 00:45:31.338
-OK, so when do I drink the tea?
-Unbelievable, man.

749
00:45:31.422 --> 00:45:33.088
Ayoob?

750
00:45:33.797 --> 00:45:37.547
If you don't want to get married, Ali...
Oh my--

751
00:45:37.630 --> 00:45:39.047
When do I drink the tea?

752
00:45:39.922 --> 00:45:41.755
No!

753
00:45:43.422 --> 00:45:45.213
Don't operate until I see her.

754
00:45:56.755 --> 00:45:58.005
And how is the play?

755
00:45:58.463 --> 00:45:59.297
Oh, excellent.

756
00:45:59.672 --> 00:46:01.463
My Ali is very gifted.

757
00:46:01.547 --> 00:46:04.713
Although his primary concern,
as you have witnessed firsthand,

758
00:46:04.797 --> 00:46:06.713
is to be a great surgeon one day.

759
00:46:06.797 --> 00:46:09.088
-That is so balanced of him.
-Indeed.

760
00:46:09.422 --> 00:46:11.005
He plays five instruments.

761
00:46:11.463 --> 00:46:12.297
I must say,

762
00:46:12.380 --> 00:46:15.297
I never thought of Saddam Hussein
as being this handsome.

763
00:46:15.380 --> 00:46:17.213
Really, it was an issue.

764
00:46:17.297 --> 00:46:20.630
Saddam was an ugly, fat man,
and my boy, well...

765
00:46:21.130 --> 00:46:23.088
-You can see with your eyes.
-Indeed.

766
00:46:23.672 --> 00:46:24.630
My own daughter.

767
00:46:24.880 --> 00:46:28.255
I wish she could hide her beauty
behind a false mustache.

768
00:46:30.172 --> 00:46:31.797
Speaking of my angel.

769
00:46:33.838 --> 00:46:35.880
-She is beautiful.
-Of course.

770
00:46:37.213 --> 00:46:38.047
Sheikhna.

771
00:46:38.463 --> 00:46:40.005
Please, try my baklava.

772
00:46:53.172 --> 00:46:54.547
Thank you, Yomna.

773
00:48:23.088 --> 00:48:25.713
He drinks the tea,
before I have given my approval.

774
00:48:28.880 --> 00:48:30.547
The boy is so eager to marry.

775
00:48:30.630 --> 00:48:31.713
It is done.

776
00:48:37.922 --> 00:48:40.797
My doctor son is engaged.

777
00:48:48.130 --> 00:48:50.505
Very unorthodox with the sugar business,

778
00:48:51.172 --> 00:48:52.005
but we are here.

779
00:49:01.172 --> 00:49:04.213
A thousand blessings
on our newly engaged couple.

780
00:49:04.630 --> 00:49:06.630
Two faiths, under one roof.

781
00:49:15.588 --> 00:49:16.422
You are quiet.

782
00:49:17.047 --> 00:49:18.880
Our son is speechless with joy.

783
00:49:19.380 --> 00:49:21.172
I will call everybody tonight.

784
00:49:21.838 --> 00:49:22.922
You liked the tea?

785
00:49:23.755 --> 00:49:24.588
It was tea.

786
00:49:25.005 --> 00:49:28.588
That will show all those women
who thought you would be single forever.

787
00:49:28.672 --> 00:49:29.505
Or worse.

788
00:49:31.630 --> 00:49:32.588
It's my degree.

789
00:49:32.672 --> 00:49:35.255
How can I be a proper husband
when I'm studying?

790
00:49:35.338 --> 00:49:38.547
You father fought in a war,
studied for two decades,

791
00:49:38.630 --> 00:49:40.588
and fathered four children
all at once.

792
00:49:40.672 --> 00:49:42.588
Mom, I'm not as good as Dad.
I need to focus.

793
00:49:42.672 --> 00:49:45.380
Maybe he is right.
After all, this is Australia.

794
00:49:45.463 --> 00:49:47.838
People only do one thing at a time.

795
00:49:48.588 --> 00:49:51.880
Perhaps I could convince Haj Karim
and the other witnesses

796
00:49:51.963 --> 00:49:53.588
to hold off the announcement.

797
00:49:53.672 --> 00:49:55.880
Maybe the end of your first year
is better.

798
00:49:57.088 --> 00:49:58.588
And you, no calls.

799
00:49:59.505 --> 00:50:00.672
Just three calls.

800
00:50:01.380 --> 00:50:02.922
No, not even half a call.

801
00:50:17.838 --> 00:50:18.838
Woman.

802
00:50:19.838 --> 00:50:22.422
The son of the cleric
says he's in tutorials with you.

803
00:50:22.505 --> 00:50:23.630
My name's Dianne.

804
00:50:23.713 --> 00:50:24.547
Is it true?

805
00:50:25.338 --> 00:50:28.047
Completely. My name is Dianne, see?

806
00:50:30.088 --> 00:50:31.338
Is it true, Dianne?

807
00:50:32.130 --> 00:50:35.797
-What, you want 100 points of ID?
-Is it true he's in tutorials with you?

808
00:50:37.047 --> 00:50:38.422
He. You mean Ali?

809
00:50:40.255 --> 00:50:41.713
What do you have against him?

810
00:50:43.672 --> 00:50:45.338
I have worked...

811
00:50:46.255 --> 00:50:48.338
day and night to get where I am.

812
00:50:49.255 --> 00:50:50.505
I deserve to be here.

813
00:50:51.380 --> 00:50:54.630
I don't like to see the son of the cleric
getting an easy ride.

814
00:50:56.047 --> 00:50:57.422
He's not a good Muslim.

815
00:50:57.922 --> 00:50:59.172
You should know that.

816
00:50:59.713 --> 00:51:01.255
So, I will ask you again...

817
00:51:01.963 --> 00:51:04.338
is he in tutorials with you,
as he says he is?

818
00:51:05.297 --> 00:51:06.130
Dianne.

819
00:51:07.880 --> 00:51:09.755
Yeah, he comes to every session.

820
00:51:10.463 --> 00:51:13.755
And he's the second smartest student
in my class, Luay.

821
00:51:27.838 --> 00:51:31.130
Why did you do the "potato pot-ah-to"
speech at the mosque?

822
00:51:34.213 --> 00:51:36.088
It was a spontaneous speech.

823
00:51:40.422 --> 00:51:42.255
You didn't get 96,4, did you?

824
00:51:48.463 --> 00:51:50.963
-It's complicated.
-What are you doing here?

825
00:51:51.213 --> 00:51:54.172
I'm doing the study, just... not enrolled.

826
00:51:54.588 --> 00:51:57.380
What, so in six years you're gonna
become a pretend doctor,

827
00:51:57.463 --> 00:51:58.797
and treat pretend patients?

828
00:51:58.880 --> 00:52:01.088
The Prophet said it's not the end result,

829
00:52:01.172 --> 00:52:02.463
it's the intention.

830
00:52:03.380 --> 00:52:04.672
I'm doing it for my dad.

831
00:52:04.755 --> 00:52:07.005
You of all people
should know what it's like.

832
00:52:07.297 --> 00:52:10.880
Dianne, ever since I was a kid,
I was introduced as Doctor Ali this,

833
00:52:10.963 --> 00:52:12.047
and Surgeon Ali that.

834
00:52:12.130 --> 00:52:14.463
I didn't have the guts to tell him
I was Moron Ali,

835
00:52:14.547 --> 00:52:16.213
and now I have to carry this.

836
00:52:16.297 --> 00:52:18.255
-A briefcase?
-It's my older brother's.

837
00:52:18.338 --> 00:52:19.547
He was the smart one.

838
00:52:19.630 --> 00:52:21.505
He should have been the great surgeon,

839
00:52:21.588 --> 00:52:24.297
but instead he had to go
and step on a fucking landmine.

840
00:52:33.422 --> 00:52:34.755
You know what? It's...

841
00:52:35.588 --> 00:52:36.588
It's my problem.

842
00:52:37.297 --> 00:52:40.047
I won't bother you with it again...

843
00:53:15.213 --> 00:53:16.297
We're out of milk.

844
00:53:17.047 --> 00:53:18.797
How about the 100 Chupa Chups?

845
00:53:26.047 --> 00:53:28.213
Charlie, do you even want to do medicine?

846
00:53:30.588 --> 00:53:31.713
It doesn't matter now.

847
00:53:35.297 --> 00:53:37.297
But, yes, I'd like to help people.

848
00:53:49.838 --> 00:53:50.797
I'll help you.

849
00:53:54.880 --> 00:53:56.130
You helped me get in.

850
00:53:57.005 --> 00:53:58.255
I'll help you get in.

851
00:54:00.588 --> 00:54:03.463
What's the most common disorder
of the autonomic nervous system

852
00:54:03.547 --> 00:54:05.505
that can impede systemic circulation?

853
00:54:05.963 --> 00:54:08.838
-I know it's not good.
-Great. What's it responsible for?

854
00:54:09.713 --> 00:54:10.547
The heart?

855
00:54:11.463 --> 00:54:15.422
Ali, the hardest thing in the world for me
has been getting in. I can't waste time.

856
00:54:15.505 --> 00:54:17.797
Tell me when you've studied it properly.

857
00:54:21.422 --> 00:54:23.255
One of the most common disorders

858
00:54:23.338 --> 00:54:26.880
is the long-standing diabetic damage
to the autonomic nerves.

859
00:54:26.963 --> 00:54:28.088
They call it the...

860
00:54:29.005 --> 00:54:30.963
diabetic autonomic neuropathy.

861
00:54:31.047 --> 00:54:34.297
Give me the physiology of what happens
to your cardiovascular system

862
00:54:34.380 --> 00:54:35.422
out of a warm bed.

863
00:54:36.755 --> 00:54:38.213
Give me to lunchtime.

864
00:54:40.130 --> 00:54:42.338
Your blood pressure would drop
immediately,

865
00:54:42.422 --> 00:54:46.047
and your heart would contract
and beat more rapidly and vigorously,

866
00:54:46.130 --> 00:54:48.213
as your arteries increase their tone,

867
00:54:48.297 --> 00:54:50.463
and then your blood pressure recovers.

868
00:54:51.838 --> 00:54:53.797
Like everyday when I see you.

869
00:55:00.213 --> 00:55:01.672
No, Dianne. I'm sorry.

870
00:55:05.255 --> 00:55:08.172
-Were you talking to her?
-Yeah, about the last lecture.

871
00:55:08.255 --> 00:55:09.922
Oh, the causes of cirrhosis?

872
00:55:10.380 --> 00:55:13.005
-What were they again?
-Why? Weren't you listening?

873
00:55:13.088 --> 00:55:15.713
Alcohol abuse, viruses, Hep A, B, C...

874
00:55:17.130 --> 00:55:19.255
No, not A, just B and C.

875
00:55:20.713 --> 00:55:22.505
I'm really sorry. That was wrong.

876
00:55:22.588 --> 00:55:24.338
I can't study with you tonight.

877
00:55:24.797 --> 00:55:25.713
I understand.

878
00:55:27.672 --> 00:55:30.130
I'm going to a film
with my basketball team.

879
00:55:31.505 --> 00:55:33.880
At 8:30. The Dorset Cinema.

880
00:56:15.588 --> 00:56:16.422
Mum.

881
00:56:16.713 --> 00:56:18.922
There's this girl at the mosque.
Quite pious.

882
00:56:19.005 --> 00:56:22.088
-She's also doing medicine.
-The chick with the English name?

883
00:56:22.172 --> 00:56:24.297
-Dianne, she's really nice.
-The Lebanese one.

884
00:56:24.380 --> 00:56:27.213
-I think her mum's Egyptian or something.
-Not Iraqi?

885
00:56:27.297 --> 00:56:29.088
I see her at uni sometimes--

886
00:56:29.172 --> 00:56:33.088
Yes, they say her father doesn't approve,
but she seems nice enough.

887
00:56:33.172 --> 00:56:34.088
Listen habibi.

888
00:56:34.172 --> 00:56:37.047
Layal, her son went to school
with Rami and Momtaz.

889
00:56:37.130 --> 00:56:39.713
She has a sinus problem.
I said you'd check it out.

890
00:56:39.797 --> 00:56:42.297
-What? I'm not a doctor yet.
-You're as good as one.

891
00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:44.422
Dianne's going to be a doctor.
She could--

892
00:56:44.505 --> 00:56:47.713
So, the antenna guy quotes us 200 bucks
to put up the aerial.

893
00:56:47.797 --> 00:56:49.338
You know what I told him?

894
00:56:49.672 --> 00:56:52.880
You're just assuming I tell him
to shove it up his ass? Anyway.

895
00:56:52.963 --> 00:56:56.005
I'll put up the aerial myself,
save you guys some cashola.

896
00:56:56.547 --> 00:56:59.088
-You are the muscles of this family.
-Thank you.

897
00:56:59.172 --> 00:57:00.755
Brains. Muscles.

898
00:57:00.838 --> 00:57:02.588
I have all the children I need.

899
00:57:02.672 --> 00:57:04.922
And my fee... Let's call it 100 bucks.

900
00:57:05.547 --> 00:57:07.797
-A hundred bucks.
-You'd be up 100 buckaroos.

901
00:57:07.880 --> 00:57:09.297
Give him $50.

902
00:57:09.380 --> 00:57:12.630
-One day I'll be out of this house.
-Dianne's surprisingly devout.

903
00:57:12.713 --> 00:57:14.505
She was born here, wasn't she?

904
00:57:15.047 --> 00:57:18.172
Yeah, but doesn't the Koran say
we're all children of one earth?

905
00:57:18.255 --> 00:57:19.922
Yes, but...

906
00:57:20.463 --> 00:57:23.755
The Koran was written
before Australia was discovered

907
00:57:23.838 --> 00:57:26.380
and the Prophet didn't know about
the beaches here.

908
00:57:26.463 --> 00:57:28.713
You know the rumors
about girls born here.

909
00:57:28.797 --> 00:57:30.005
I was born here.

910
00:57:30.922 --> 00:57:33.922
Your sister.
She has seen things beyond her age.

911
00:57:34.005 --> 00:57:37.963
Men, in bathers. People kissing on TV.

912
00:57:38.047 --> 00:57:39.380
I can still hear you.

913
00:57:39.463 --> 00:57:41.088
-Mohammed!
-Yeah, Mum.

914
00:57:41.172 --> 00:57:43.588
Get your sister
to help you with the antenna.

915
00:57:43.672 --> 00:57:45.630
I'm not going on the roof
with that lunatic.

916
00:57:45.713 --> 00:57:46.922
Mum, Dianne's different.

917
00:57:47.005 --> 00:57:48.672
Ali, habibi.

918
00:57:49.005 --> 00:57:51.672
Girls brought up here
are like our dishwasher.

919
00:57:51.838 --> 00:57:53.922
We thought we were buying it brand new,

920
00:57:54.005 --> 00:57:55.380
until we found out...

921
00:57:55.463 --> 00:57:57.130
it was a floor model.

922
00:57:57.630 --> 00:57:59.880
And she is not right for your brother.

923
00:58:00.380 --> 00:58:01.213
For Moe?

924
00:58:01.297 --> 00:58:03.505
Enough. She's Lebanese.

925
00:58:05.588 --> 00:58:06.797
Ramona, get up here.

926
00:58:08.297 --> 00:58:09.713
You call yourself fit?

927
00:58:10.255 --> 00:58:13.463
If I was the coach, I'd get you all
to strip naked in the desert

928
00:58:13.547 --> 00:58:14.755
and run like donkeys.

929
00:58:16.338 --> 00:58:17.713
What are you doing?

930
00:58:20.338 --> 00:58:21.255
I've got to go.

931
00:58:22.130 --> 00:58:23.463
I've got to study.

932
00:58:23.880 --> 00:58:25.922
The oil in the fryer needs changing.

933
00:58:26.005 --> 00:58:27.213
We never change it.

934
00:58:27.880 --> 00:58:29.588
Customers need to be served.

935
00:58:29.922 --> 00:58:32.963
If I change the oil now,
and serve all night, can I go?

936
00:58:35.005 --> 00:58:36.713
Please. I'll be back by eight.

937
00:58:37.672 --> 00:58:39.297
I'll make you Mum's tagine.

938
00:58:40.922 --> 00:58:41.755
Yeah?

939
00:58:42.422 --> 00:58:44.380
Everything now and back by seven.

940
00:58:44.755 --> 00:58:45.713
Thank you.

941
00:58:45.797 --> 00:58:46.922
I love you, Dad.

942
00:58:47.547 --> 00:58:48.463
No smoking.

943
00:58:48.880 --> 00:58:49.713
I know.

944
00:58:51.422 --> 00:58:52.380
God help me.

945
00:58:54.838 --> 00:58:57.963
I could never tell my Dad we speak speak,
could you?

946
00:58:58.797 --> 00:59:00.630
Mum's funny about the Lebanese.

947
00:59:00.838 --> 00:59:04.588
My dad thinks Iraqis are the source
of all the misery in the Middle East.

948
00:59:05.255 --> 00:59:06.088
Oh.

949
00:59:06.963 --> 00:59:10.172
My mum just reckons
you guys ruin Middle Eastern food.

950
00:59:12.255 --> 00:59:13.755
I don't know what I want.

951
00:59:19.213 --> 00:59:20.047
I do.

952
00:59:26.047 --> 00:59:27.422
It's so beautiful here.

953
00:59:32.755 --> 00:59:35.713
You know, this is as much
as we can ever do.

954
00:59:38.630 --> 00:59:39.463
Yes, I know.

955
01:00:05.755 --> 01:00:08.213
Leave them be. They are young.

956
01:00:08.588 --> 01:00:11.213
Let his hands wander
as long as seed is not spilled.

957
01:00:16.880 --> 01:00:18.338
Good. Apart.

958
01:00:18.880 --> 01:00:20.797
We're a very modern family here.

959
01:00:21.672 --> 01:00:23.713
I'll be downstairs if you need...

960
01:00:25.755 --> 01:00:28.172
Are you trying to give me diabetes?

961
01:00:29.338 --> 01:00:32.172
-I heard you have a sweet tooth.
-I don't have a sweet tooth.

962
01:00:32.255 --> 01:00:34.422
How many children do you want?

963
01:00:34.963 --> 01:00:36.922
As many as makes you happy.

964
01:00:37.713 --> 01:00:39.172
Good. Then none.

965
01:00:40.797 --> 01:00:41.672
What? Really?

966
01:00:42.463 --> 01:00:43.380
I hate children.

967
01:00:45.255 --> 01:00:46.547
They can be annoying.

968
01:00:47.088 --> 01:00:50.047
They cost too much.
So many nappies. Disgusting.

969
01:00:50.130 --> 01:00:51.047
And you know what?

970
01:00:51.130 --> 01:00:53.838
I think I might give up medicine.

971
01:00:54.213 --> 01:00:56.172
Just sit and watch TV all day.

972
01:00:56.630 --> 01:00:57.463
Cricket.

973
01:00:57.963 --> 01:00:58.922
Test match cricket.

974
01:01:00.172 --> 01:01:03.422
Also, I'm going to eat and get fat.

975
01:01:03.505 --> 01:01:06.213
And I mean reality-show fat.

976
01:01:07.255 --> 01:01:10.172
Well, as long as you're comfortable,
I will be too.

977
01:01:10.672 --> 01:01:14.672
Rings from the finest jewelers,

978
01:01:15.047 --> 01:01:17.755
our gold plucked from the desert sands--

979
01:01:17.838 --> 01:01:18.963
Too expensive.

980
01:01:23.088 --> 01:01:26.463
I forget you are but a student,
saving for the future.

981
01:01:34.963 --> 01:01:36.797
What are you trying to tell me, Ali?

982
01:01:43.630 --> 01:01:44.463
Two.

983
01:01:47.422 --> 01:01:48.547
I'd want two kids.

984
01:01:50.713 --> 01:01:51.755
At least.

985
01:01:53.005 --> 01:01:54.797
And three sugars.

986
01:01:55.838 --> 01:01:57.922
So this chick you're saddled with?

987
01:01:58.797 --> 01:02:00.713
-She's a dog?
-No.

988
01:02:01.213 --> 01:02:03.422
She's beautiful. Nice, too.

989
01:02:03.505 --> 01:02:06.172
-I'm struggling to see the problem.
-She's not the one.

990
01:02:06.255 --> 01:02:08.588
Well then, who is? Not that medical chick?

991
01:02:10.088 --> 01:02:12.797
Unbelievable, man.
How could you keep this from us?

992
01:02:12.880 --> 01:02:14.130
-You animal.
-It's weird.

993
01:02:14.463 --> 01:02:16.922
When I'm with Dianne,
I feel like I'm me, you know?

994
01:02:17.005 --> 01:02:18.630
It's weird because you're engaged.

995
01:02:18.713 --> 01:02:20.713
You can't be seen together
or speak to her.

996
01:02:20.963 --> 01:02:23.338
-Does Dianne know you're engaged?
-Of course not.

997
01:02:23.422 --> 01:02:25.130
-Call off the engagement.
-I can't.

998
01:02:25.213 --> 01:02:27.588
-What would people say? Your father?
-I know.

999
01:02:27.672 --> 01:02:29.130
Moussa’s mum, remember?

1000
01:02:29.213 --> 01:02:31.213
Two weeks in hospital
after he called it off.

1001
01:02:31.297 --> 01:02:34.297
-Double unbelievable.
-Can't you guys have, like, 72 wives?

1002
01:02:35.463 --> 01:02:39.380
♪ They think they can beat him
They lie to themselves♪

1003
01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:43.088
♪ While they try to bomb him
He plays with our girls♪

1004
01:02:43.172 --> 01:02:46.463
♪ While Iraq burns
He plays with two girls♪

1005
01:02:47.297 --> 01:02:48.213
Forgot your gun.

1006
01:02:48.297 --> 01:02:49.380
Only two?

1007
01:02:49.630 --> 01:02:51.922
You know how many wives
Saddam actually had?

1008
01:02:52.463 --> 01:02:53.297
More than you?

1009
01:02:53.380 --> 01:02:56.505
1,300. Temporary marriages, of course.

1010
01:02:56.588 --> 01:02:59.005
-Are temporary marriages even real?
-Of course!

1011
01:02:59.672 --> 01:03:04.630
I spent my teenage years
studying Koranic jurisprudence.

1012
01:03:05.130 --> 01:03:06.630
Some you marry for one hour,

1013
01:03:06.713 --> 01:03:08.505
some for a day,

1014
01:03:08.588 --> 01:03:11.547
and the ones with stamina, like a taxi...

1015
01:03:12.755 --> 01:03:13.963
you leave the meter on.

1016
01:03:14.047 --> 01:03:15.713
Cue Saddam Hussein.

1017
01:03:16.672 --> 01:03:18.755
If temporary marriages were real,

1018
01:03:19.130 --> 01:03:20.755
why don't all Muslims do it?

1019
01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:24.338
They don't know Islamic laws like I do.

1020
01:03:25.588 --> 01:03:26.963
There is always a loophole.

1021
01:03:27.047 --> 01:03:29.213
Cue Saddam Hussein 20 minutes ago.

1022
01:03:38.838 --> 01:03:40.588
What are you doing here? Go away.

1023
01:03:40.672 --> 01:03:42.588
I found a way we can be together.

1024
01:03:42.963 --> 01:03:44.130
Temporary marriage.

1025
01:03:44.713 --> 01:03:47.297
Temporary marriage?
You came here just to say that?

1026
01:03:47.380 --> 01:03:49.672
Come on.
That's just a loophole for horny Arabs.

1027
01:03:49.755 --> 01:03:51.838
Yeah, but it's written law.

1028
01:03:52.213 --> 01:03:54.463
"A man who desireth temporary marriage,

1029
01:03:54.547 --> 01:03:57.838
must first set a reasonable time limit,
reasonable dowry,

1030
01:03:57.922 --> 01:03:59.713
treat the woman with dignity..."

1031
01:03:59.797 --> 01:04:00.797
I'm all about that.

1032
01:04:01.213 --> 01:04:03.547
It's not in the Koran.
It's not in the text.

1033
01:04:03.630 --> 01:04:04.713
Yeah, but it's here.

1034
01:04:04.797 --> 01:04:07.088
It means
we can have a proper relationship.

1035
01:04:07.672 --> 01:04:09.213
But, you know? Temporary.

1036
01:04:09.588 --> 01:04:10.630
Like Australians.

1037
01:04:10.838 --> 01:04:12.380
What are you two talking about?

1038
01:04:12.463 --> 01:04:15.505
Your daughter's asking me
about a possible cure for arthritis.

1039
01:04:15.838 --> 01:04:16.713
Yalla, OK.

1040
01:04:20.963 --> 01:04:23.380
Jewell Station tomorrow at eleven o'clock.

1041
01:04:23.463 --> 01:04:24.297
OK?

1042
01:04:25.213 --> 01:04:26.838
Go. Go on.

1043
01:04:45.338 --> 01:04:47.963
I haven't got long.
I'm supposed to be delivering these.

1044
01:04:48.047 --> 01:04:49.005
How does this work?

1045
01:04:50.088 --> 01:04:50.922
I don't know.

1046
01:04:51.838 --> 01:04:55.088
But once we get married
we could... do things.

1047
01:04:55.172 --> 01:04:56.713
I could say things to you.

1048
01:04:57.297 --> 01:04:58.630
We can say things now.

1049
01:04:58.963 --> 01:05:00.922
No, like when we're alone.

1050
01:05:01.088 --> 01:05:02.255
I could say I like you,

1051
01:05:02.338 --> 01:05:04.880
and if you felt like it,
you could say you like me.

1052
01:05:04.963 --> 01:05:07.838
OK, apart from standing around
telling each other we like each other,

1053
01:05:07.922 --> 01:05:09.130
what else can we do?

1054
01:05:13.838 --> 01:05:15.088
We could go bowling.

1055
01:05:17.338 --> 01:05:18.755
OK, we could go bowling.

1056
01:05:20.088 --> 01:05:23.422
We could have ice cream together.
We could go to the aquarium.

1057
01:05:23.588 --> 01:05:24.963
We could watch another movie.

1058
01:05:25.047 --> 01:05:27.338
I could put my arm around your waist
this time.

1059
01:05:27.422 --> 01:05:28.838
How long would we be married?

1060
01:05:29.672 --> 01:05:30.922
Medicine's six years.

1061
01:05:31.005 --> 01:05:33.797
-How about we start with six weeks?
-Sure. Great.

1062
01:05:34.422 --> 01:05:35.255
OK.

1063
01:05:36.422 --> 01:05:37.630
But no one can know.

1064
01:05:37.797 --> 01:05:39.588
I think we need two witnesses.

1065
01:05:47.047 --> 01:05:48.130
You look beautiful.

1066
01:05:48.213 --> 01:05:50.380
OK, say your vows.
We're gonna catch the next train.

1067
01:05:50.463 --> 01:05:51.713
OK. I, Ali Dianne...

1068
01:05:53.005 --> 01:05:55.005
I, Ali Albasri, take Dianne Mohsen,

1069
01:05:55.088 --> 01:05:57.713
to be my religiously lawfully wedded wife.

1070
01:05:57.797 --> 01:06:00.130
-Her dowry being...
-The fish and chips will do.

1071
01:06:00.213 --> 01:06:02.380
-Her dowry being 200 grams of snapper.
-Flake.

1072
01:06:02.463 --> 01:06:04.797
-You don't want the snapper at our place.
-Quick.

1073
01:06:05.130 --> 01:06:06.255
So, do you take me?

1074
01:06:06.380 --> 01:06:07.213
I do.

1075
01:06:07.588 --> 01:06:08.422
For six weeks.

1076
01:06:09.297 --> 01:06:12.088
-We've witnessed this solemn proceeding.
-So, kiss her.

1077
01:06:23.213 --> 01:06:25.463
We should give
this temporary marriage thing a go.

1078
01:06:33.088 --> 01:06:36.797
I will never, ever be caught.

1079
01:06:37.255 --> 01:06:38.338
Yeah!

1080
01:06:38.963 --> 01:06:41.797
♪ Master Saddam stay defiant♪

1081
01:06:42.213 --> 01:06:45.422
♪ You will never be caught♪

1082
01:06:45.588 --> 01:06:48.630
♪ Let the US and their allies♪

1083
01:06:48.713 --> 01:06:51.547
♪ Come attacking
I have backing♪

1084
01:06:52.547 --> 01:06:55.588
♪ Yes, yes, master
We have your back♪

1085
01:06:55.672 --> 01:06:58.505
♪ No, no, Saddam
We will attack♪

1086
01:06:59.297 --> 01:07:01.172
All your secrets will be open.

1087
01:07:02.088 --> 01:07:05.338
Master Saddam, the Americans crashed
through the gates. We must run.

1088
01:07:06.922 --> 01:07:07.755
What happened?

1089
01:07:08.547 --> 01:07:10.047
No!

1090
01:07:10.130 --> 01:07:11.755
Allahu Akbar.

1091
01:07:11.838 --> 01:07:13.380
Come on, Saddam.

1092
01:07:13.963 --> 01:07:16.755
Nuke them with your might and power.

1093
01:07:19.505 --> 01:07:22.463
There are no WMDs.

1094
01:07:23.005 --> 01:07:25.047
I had to fake it...

1095
01:07:25.380 --> 01:07:27.047
Till I make it.

1096
01:07:27.172 --> 01:07:29.880
♪ All these years he lied to us♪

1097
01:07:30.255 --> 01:07:32.713
♪ He lied to us
He lied to us♪

1098
01:07:33.047 --> 01:07:35.463
No. It cannot end like this.

1099
01:07:36.672 --> 01:07:39.422
♪ You will be caught
You will be caught♪

1100
01:07:39.505 --> 01:07:42.755
♪ You will be caught
You will be caught♪

1101
01:07:42.838 --> 01:07:45.755
♪ You will be caught♪

1102
01:07:52.463 --> 01:07:53.922
We're going to Broadway.

1103
01:07:54.005 --> 01:07:55.838
Broadway? Unbelievable, man.

1104
01:07:55.963 --> 01:07:56.797
No!

1105
01:08:00.588 --> 01:08:02.255
No one said Broadway.

1106
01:08:02.838 --> 01:08:05.422
It is the Bin Khattabi multipurpose hall.

1107
01:08:05.838 --> 01:08:07.838
How does that even sound like Broadway?

1108
01:08:07.922 --> 01:08:10.797
It is a Muslim community hall in Detroit.

1109
01:08:10.880 --> 01:08:12.172
We're going to Detroit?

1110
01:08:12.255 --> 01:08:14.880
-Detroit. Unbelievable, man.
-Yes.

1111
01:08:15.588 --> 01:08:18.130
Our dear friend, Dr. Hasoon Albandar...

1112
01:08:18.213 --> 01:08:21.755
He is the brother-in-law
to the Iraqi ambassador in the US.

1113
01:08:22.380 --> 01:08:23.838
He saw the show and loved it.

1114
01:08:23.922 --> 01:08:25.088
He made one phone call

1115
01:08:25.172 --> 01:08:28.297
and we have been invited to perform it
live in Detroit

1116
01:08:32.797 --> 01:08:37.588
Sheikhna, won't that mean we'll be serving
the devil regime of the USA?

1117
01:08:38.588 --> 01:08:41.047
Luay will not be needed.
Principal cast only.

1118
01:08:41.130 --> 01:08:44.297
So your conscience can remain guilt-free,
Seyyed.

1119
01:08:47.213 --> 01:08:48.713
I'm not going to Detroit?

1120
01:08:58.130 --> 01:08:59.255
Bro, the mustache.

1121
01:09:18.922 --> 01:09:20.297
You've got your hair out.

1122
01:09:20.380 --> 01:09:22.338
And you've got a stupid mustache.

1123
01:09:22.422 --> 01:09:23.672
Oh yeah. Hey, listen.

1124
01:09:23.963 --> 01:09:26.713
-I found a way for us to stay together.
-We are together.

1125
01:09:26.797 --> 01:09:28.630
No, together together. Forever.

1126
01:09:28.963 --> 01:09:30.672
The play's going to America.

1127
01:09:30.755 --> 01:09:31.630
-What?
-Yeah.

1128
01:09:31.713 --> 01:09:32.630
That's amazing.

1129
01:09:33.047 --> 01:09:34.630
-You are so good.
-Really?

1130
01:09:34.713 --> 01:09:35.797
I was really proud.

1131
01:09:35.880 --> 01:09:38.130
This is God,
the author of destinies and will.

1132
01:09:38.213 --> 01:09:40.713
He's talking to me.
He's laying out the path for us.

1133
01:09:40.797 --> 01:09:43.130
-Slow down, Charlie.
-God wants me to disappear.

1134
01:09:43.213 --> 01:09:46.088
In the States, I'm going to call Dad,
away from the mosque,

1135
01:09:46.172 --> 01:09:47.338
away from the community.

1136
01:09:47.422 --> 01:09:50.797
I'm gonna tell him the truth.
I'm gonna stay there and not come back.

1137
01:09:50.880 --> 01:09:53.422
-I don't want you to go.
-No, hear me out.

1138
01:09:53.505 --> 01:09:56.338
-I'll drop medicine--
-You were never doing medicine.

1139
01:09:56.422 --> 01:09:58.505
I'm going to get work there, as an actor.

1140
01:09:58.588 --> 01:10:01.463
Hollywood always needs people like us
to play terrorists.

1141
01:10:01.672 --> 01:10:03.130
And then you can join me.

1142
01:10:03.213 --> 01:10:04.630
You come over, we get married,

1143
01:10:04.713 --> 01:10:06.922
and we stay there
until our parents forgive us.

1144
01:10:07.005 --> 01:10:09.338
This sounds like one of your plans.
We can't just run away.

1145
01:10:10.380 --> 01:10:13.380
-I'm not turning my back on medicine.
-No, you mustn't.

1146
01:10:13.463 --> 01:10:15.963
There's great medical schools there.

1147
01:10:21.880 --> 01:10:24.172
-This is insane.
-No, it's more than insane.

1148
01:10:24.255 --> 01:10:26.338
But we're Muslim.
What other options have we got?

1149
01:10:26.838 --> 01:10:28.755
In America we can live like Australians.

1150
01:10:32.963 --> 01:10:35.255
Do you really want to be with me forever?

1151
01:10:39.172 --> 01:10:40.172
Please don't.

1152
01:10:41.172 --> 01:10:42.547
Please. Charlie...

1153
01:10:42.797 --> 01:10:45.005
Dianne. I want to marry you.

1154
01:10:46.297 --> 01:10:47.505
And not temporary.

1155
01:10:47.963 --> 01:10:48.797
Shit.

1156
01:10:48.880 --> 01:10:50.005
-What?
-Fish bone.

1157
01:10:51.505 --> 01:10:52.338
Dianne.

1158
01:10:53.130 --> 01:10:55.880
I've never known, ever,
what I've wanted, but...

1159
01:10:56.963 --> 01:10:57.838
This I know.

1160
01:10:59.380 --> 01:11:00.922
Don't you want to marry me?

1161
01:11:01.005 --> 01:11:03.255
What have you done with my glasses?

1162
01:11:03.338 --> 01:11:05.047
They'll be on his stupid head.

1163
01:11:05.130 --> 01:11:06.797
Please, just think about it.

1164
01:11:45.713 --> 01:11:47.713
I'll call you as soon as I've settled.

1165
01:11:56.172 --> 01:11:57.588
Tell us one more time.

1166
01:11:57.672 --> 01:11:59.588
We like hearing your Aussie accent.

1167
01:11:59.672 --> 01:12:02.963
How many times do I have to tell you?
It's a musical, a comedy.

1168
01:12:03.047 --> 01:12:05.047
It's a funny play about Saddam Hussein.

1169
01:12:05.130 --> 01:12:07.588
-We don't tend to laugh at terrorism.
-Terrorism?

1170
01:12:08.088 --> 01:12:09.213
It's on your phone.

1171
01:12:13.255 --> 01:12:15.547
What have you guys planted on my phone?

1172
01:12:15.838 --> 01:12:17.755
"We will come back and kill them."

1173
01:12:20.255 --> 01:12:21.380
That's not mine.

1174
01:12:22.422 --> 01:12:23.255
Your words.

1175
01:12:24.713 --> 01:12:26.255
"I'll have front row seats."

1176
01:12:27.755 --> 01:12:29.713
-What?
-"I will watch them suffer."

1177
01:12:30.255 --> 01:12:34.255
"The bombers will slaughter you."
Should I keep reading this obscenity?

1178
01:12:34.588 --> 01:12:35.588
Name the bombers.

1179
01:12:36.463 --> 01:12:38.088
The Bombers.

1180
01:12:38.838 --> 01:12:40.922
The Bombers are a footie team.

1181
01:12:41.255 --> 01:12:42.088
AFL.

1182
01:12:42.505 --> 01:12:45.338
Aussie rules. You guys have NFL here.
We've got AFL.

1183
01:12:45.422 --> 01:12:48.172
Those were text messages
I sent to my mate, Wazza.

1184
01:12:48.255 --> 01:12:49.922
Because he's an idiot Magpie fan.

1185
01:12:50.005 --> 01:12:51.922
Got to admire the guile of these guys.

1186
01:12:52.338 --> 01:12:54.630
They concoct a pro-American play,

1187
01:12:54.713 --> 01:12:57.922
sell out to a thousand crazed zealots
in Detroit,

1188
01:12:58.005 --> 01:13:01.213
and then hide
all their sicko terrorist messages

1189
01:13:01.297 --> 01:13:02.880
behind a football team.

1190
01:13:03.672 --> 01:13:04.505
Wow.

1191
01:13:05.380 --> 01:13:06.255
No.

1192
01:13:06.630 --> 01:13:09.213
I've got to be in Detroit.
I've got to disappear.

1193
01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:10.922
It's God's plan.

1194
01:13:13.672 --> 01:13:16.297
Ladies and gentlemen,
this is your captain speaking.

1195
01:13:16.547 --> 01:13:18.088
I'll ask you to fasten your seat belts.

1196
01:13:18.172 --> 01:13:20.547
We'll have turbulence
on our descent into Melbourne.

1197
01:13:20.630 --> 01:13:22.713
A few bumps ahead, I'm afraid.

1198
01:13:43.422 --> 01:13:44.255
Ali.

1199
01:13:51.630 --> 01:13:54.172
I will ask you this once and once only.

1200
01:13:55.130 --> 01:13:57.047
All I want is a straight answer.

1201
01:14:00.172 --> 01:14:01.547
Are you doing medicine?

1202
01:14:07.422 --> 01:14:10.088
Did you get the score
you told everyone you got?

1203
01:14:10.172 --> 01:14:12.838
Sheikhna, don't be too hard on the boy.

1204
01:14:13.172 --> 01:14:15.547
I was trying to let them know
you were overseas

1205
01:14:15.630 --> 01:14:17.588
and they told me you weren't enrolled.

1206
01:14:17.672 --> 01:14:20.880
So naturally we thought
that there must be a mistake.

1207
01:14:21.463 --> 01:14:22.547
But, alas.

1208
01:14:23.047 --> 01:14:26.255
When have I given you the impression
I am your enemy?

1209
01:14:27.630 --> 01:14:29.255
Or worse, a dictator?

1210
01:14:29.630 --> 01:14:30.463
Or...

1211
01:14:32.797 --> 01:14:35.505
You couldn't come to me
and tell me straight?

1212
01:14:36.838 --> 01:14:37.672
"Dad.

1213
01:14:38.005 --> 01:14:39.213
I failed. I'm sorry.

1214
01:14:39.630 --> 01:14:41.297
I tried, but not to be."

1215
01:14:42.505 --> 01:14:44.463
-I'm sorry, Dad.
-Sorry, nothing.

1216
01:14:45.047 --> 01:14:47.172
You will apologize to the community.

1217
01:14:48.422 --> 01:14:49.297
I am done.

1218
01:15:01.130 --> 01:15:05.380
The Prophet has said
that lying is a sin,

1219
01:15:06.213 --> 01:15:10.588
which burns away at the soul
as fire burns through wood.

1220
01:15:16.588 --> 01:15:17.422
Hence,

1221
01:15:18.547 --> 01:15:20.213
I stand before you,

1222
01:15:21.088 --> 01:15:22.338
and before God,

1223
01:15:26.380 --> 01:15:28.088
offering my repentance.

1224
01:15:33.838 --> 01:15:35.838
Assalamu 'Alaikum.

1225
01:15:39.797 --> 01:15:41.005
We've now heard it.

1226
01:15:41.630 --> 01:15:44.547
Where to now? I hear everyone ask.

1227
01:15:46.838 --> 01:15:50.380
Sheikh Mahdi has done a reasonable job
raising his children.

1228
01:15:51.005 --> 01:15:55.422
I don't see the need
for our sheikh to step down immediately.

1229
01:15:56.630 --> 01:16:00.380
However, if my son
had been a lying failure,

1230
01:16:00.463 --> 01:16:03.713
I know in my heart,
I could not live with the shame.

1231
01:16:03.797 --> 01:16:06.672
Sheikhna, what if the boy gets married?

1232
01:16:07.172 --> 01:16:09.047
To atone and prove he is a man.

1233
01:16:10.505 --> 01:16:12.505
Abu Faisal.

1234
01:16:13.297 --> 01:16:14.130
Please.

1235
01:16:16.755 --> 01:16:18.297
It is with great pain,

1236
01:16:19.880 --> 01:16:21.797
I must reveal another,

1237
01:16:22.338 --> 01:16:24.213
yet more shocking truth.

1238
01:16:24.922 --> 01:16:26.922
I, unwittingly,

1239
01:16:27.713 --> 01:16:29.047
while driving my taxi,

1240
01:16:29.380 --> 01:16:32.630
stumbled upon Ali
with a loose Muslim woman,

1241
01:16:32.713 --> 01:16:36.463
at places not consistent
with our religion.

1242
01:16:37.047 --> 01:16:38.088
A bowling alley.

1243
01:16:38.797 --> 01:16:39.880
An aquarium.

1244
01:16:40.547 --> 01:16:43.922
The picture resolution is not perfect,
but if you zoom in...

1245
01:16:45.713 --> 01:16:48.088
What is this fool on about?
Tell me this was not you.

1246
01:16:48.713 --> 01:16:49.547
No!

1247
01:16:50.005 --> 01:16:50.880
Haj Karim.

1248
01:16:51.588 --> 01:16:54.547
You offered Ali
your daughter's hand in marriage,

1249
01:16:54.797 --> 01:16:57.422
and he has betrayed her
with another woman.

1250
01:16:58.630 --> 01:17:00.547
It helps no one to name names.

1251
01:17:01.047 --> 01:17:02.588
The girl knows who she is.

1252
01:17:02.922 --> 01:17:06.297
That's what happens
when we let our women go to university.

1253
01:17:06.422 --> 01:17:10.005
Seyyed, please.
Why are you doing this to her?

1254
01:17:10.797 --> 01:17:13.422
Please, sir.
It's not her fault. Please.

1255
01:17:13.797 --> 01:17:14.630
I beg you.

1256
01:17:14.838 --> 01:17:16.838
Nothing improper happened.
She's guiltless.

1257
01:17:16.922 --> 01:17:17.755
I trusted you.

1258
01:17:18.755 --> 01:17:19.588
You've shamed me.

1259
01:17:19.672 --> 01:17:20.505
It's not her fault.

1260
01:17:20.588 --> 01:17:21.630
You've shamed me.

1261
01:17:21.713 --> 01:17:23.338
I think you have said enough.

1262
01:17:36.588 --> 01:17:37.422
Dianne, wait.

1263
01:17:38.338 --> 01:17:39.922
I've never touched Yomna.

1264
01:17:40.172 --> 01:17:42.922
My parents, the community...
They all arranged it for me.

1265
01:17:43.005 --> 01:17:43.838
Believe me.

1266
01:17:43.922 --> 01:17:45.422
Why would I do that?

1267
01:17:45.505 --> 01:17:48.838
You've told so many lies,
you have no soul left.

1268
01:17:49.213 --> 01:17:51.130
Everything about you is just a lie.

1269
01:17:51.213 --> 01:17:53.172
No, everything except you is a lie.

1270
01:17:53.255 --> 01:17:55.005
Do you get what you've done, Ali?

1271
01:17:55.088 --> 01:17:56.797
I can't do medicine.

1272
01:17:56.880 --> 01:17:59.172
He's going to send me back to Lebanon.

1273
01:17:59.255 --> 01:18:00.672
You have fucked up my life.

1274
01:18:00.755 --> 01:18:03.380
-OK. I'll talk to your dad.
-You've fucked up my life.

1275
01:18:03.463 --> 01:18:05.380
Don't talk to anyone, ever.

1276
01:18:05.797 --> 01:18:08.047
Sit in a cave for the rest of your life.

1277
01:18:08.130 --> 01:18:10.338
-Just leave me the fuck alone.
-But I love you.

1278
01:18:10.838 --> 01:18:13.088
I absolutely hate you. I hate you.

1279
01:18:13.172 --> 01:18:15.088
I hate you. I divorce you.

1280
01:18:15.172 --> 01:18:17.422
I divorce you. I divorce you.

1281
01:18:18.005 --> 01:18:21.380
I divorce you.
I divorce you a thousand times.

1282
01:18:25.047 --> 01:18:26.880
That's one continuous thought.

1283
01:18:47.213 --> 01:18:49.672
All this madness will soon be behind us.

1284
01:18:52.588 --> 01:18:54.422
Let's just get through the day.

1285
01:18:55.797 --> 01:18:56.630
Good boy.

1286
01:19:03.380 --> 01:19:05.797
Prove yourself a worthy husband to Yomna,

1287
01:19:06.380 --> 01:19:07.880
and all will be forgiven.

1288
01:19:08.380 --> 01:19:10.630
Not many girls would have forgiven you.

1289
01:19:10.713 --> 01:19:14.838
She has accepted
you just knew the Lebanese from uni.

1290
01:19:17.922 --> 01:19:18.755
Mohammed.

1291
01:19:19.172 --> 01:19:20.547
-Yeah, Mum.
-Inside.

1292
01:19:20.755 --> 01:19:22.172
Are you going to be OK?

1293
01:19:31.880 --> 01:19:33.380
Ali, you're in luck.

1294
01:19:33.463 --> 01:19:36.463
My dad just bought a second-hand taxi.
The night shift's yours.

1295
01:19:36.547 --> 01:19:38.755
In two years' time,
you could have the day shift.

1296
01:19:39.213 --> 01:19:40.047
Thanks, Ayoob.

1297
01:19:40.172 --> 01:19:41.922
Hey, Az, it's a good turnout.

1298
01:19:42.338 --> 01:19:45.547
I might say hello to your old man.
What do I say? Your holiness?

1299
01:19:45.630 --> 01:19:46.463
Just say hi.

1300
01:19:47.547 --> 01:19:50.380
Take one tablet, an hour before bed.

1301
01:19:51.755 --> 01:19:53.005
